(/tahoma/consent/issues/682)) and precede package/library resolution ([#50](/tahoma/consent/issues/50)), so the resolver consumes provider declarations and extension points instead of enumerating every agent, SRFI, and host-adapter primitive surface itself.\n- Library resolution ([#50](/tahoma/consent/issues/50)) should follow [#483](/tahoma/consent/issues/483), [#484](/tahoma/consent/issues/484), [#682](/tahoma/consent/issues/682), and [#681](/tahoma/consent/issues/681), define SRFI import names and shims before the vendored SRFI bundle ([#54](/tahoma/consent/issues/54)) is integrated broadly, and consume provider-owned primitive-library registration rather than owning domain primitive specs.\n- Vendored SRFI bundle tracking ([#54](/tahoma/consent/issues/54)) is promoted into Chunk 0.18 ahead of the long-tail SRFI pool (Chunk S) because it is the bundle-level contract that the substrate SRFI promotions and outward protocol libraries ([#57](/tahoma/consent/issues/57)) depend on.\n- Self-hostable portable numeric backend work ([#350](/tahoma/consent/issues/350)) should follow numeric tower (~~[#16](/tahoma/consent/issues/16)~~), native inexact ownership (~~[#84](/tahoma/consent/issues/84)~~), and multi-host bootstrap framing (~~[#55](/tahoma/consent/issues/55)~~), is promoted into the Tangerine chunk (0.21) because fixnums/flonums and the finalized Tangerine numeric tower depend on it, defines which host numeric operations are semantic blockers versus temporary accelerators, and feeds the later compiled runtime ABI and allocation/GC contract ([#120](/tahoma/consent/issues/120) and [#333](/tahoma/consent/issues/333)).\n- Portable character model ownership ([#349](/tahoma/consent/issues/349)) should follow core data and writer behavior (~~[#17](/tahoma/consent/issues/17)~~), multi-host bootstrap framing (~~[#55](/tahoma/consent/issues/55)~~), and character externalization parity (~~[#83](/tahoma/consent/issues/83)~~), is placed in the pre-1.0 portable bootstrap ownership chunk (0.32) rather than backfilled into the historical core chunk, and defines Consent Scheme-owned character and Unicode behavior rather than host R7RS behavior.\n- Portable symbol identity ownership ([#346](/tahoma/consent/issues/346)) should follow core data and writer behavior (~~[#17](/tahoma/consent/issues/17)~~) and multi-host bootstrap framing (~~[#55](/tahoma/consent/issues/55)~~), is placed in the pre-1.0 portable bootstrap ownership chunk (0.32) rather than backfilled into the historical core chunk, ensures portable reader/evaluator/macro/library code uses Consent Scheme-owned symbol datums instead of host-native symbols, and feeds the compound datum and equivalence follow-ups ([#347](/tahoma/consent/issues/347) and [#348](/tahoma/consent/issues/348)).\n- Portable compound datum heap ownership ([#347](/tahoma/consent/issues/347)) should follow core data and writer behavior (~~[#17](/tahoma/consent/issues/17)~~), multi-host bootstrap framing (~~[#55](/tahoma/consent/issues/55)~~), and portable symbol identity ownership ([#346](/tahoma/consent/issues/346)), is placed in the pre-1.0 portable bootstrap ownership chunk (0.32) rather than backfilled into the historical core chunk, ensures pairs, strings, vectors, bytevectors, mutation, cycles, and shared structure are represented by Consent Scheme-owned objects rather than host-native datums, and precedes equivalence cleanup ([#348](/tahoma/consent/issues/348)).\n- Portable equivalence cleanup ([#348](/tahoma/consent/issues/348)) should follow numeric tower work (~~[#16](/tahoma/consent/issues/16)~~ and ~~[#84](/tahoma/consent/issues/84)~~), core data and writer behavior (~~[#17](/tahoma/consent/issues/17)~~), multi-host bootstrap framing (~~[#55](/tahoma/consent/issues/55)~~), portable symbol identity ownership ([#346](/tahoma/consent/issues/346)), and the owned compound datum heap ([#347](/tahoma/consent/issues/347)), is placed in the pre-1.0 portable bootstrap ownership chunk (0.32) rather than backfilled into the historical core chunk, and replaces host `eq?`/`eqv?` fallbacks with Consent Scheme-owned value identity.\n- R7RS-small compliance (~~[#19](/tahoma/consent/issues/19)~~) should remain distinct from optional SRFI support ([#54](/tahoma/consent/issues/54)). Portable bootstrap blocker follow-ups ([#346](/tahoma/consent/issues/346) through [#351](/tahoma/consent/issues/351)) are post-core ownership work placed in the pre-1.0 portable bootstrap ownership chunk (0.32) rather than prerequisites backfilled into the historical core chunk.\n- Vendored SRFI bundle work ([#54](/tahoma/consent/issues/54)) should follow library resolution ([#50](/tahoma/consent/issues/50)) and helper self-tests (~~[#31](/tahoma/consent/issues/31)~~); import naming and feature-conditional setup should precede scheduled SRFI libraries, dependency shims should precede the libraries that need them, and SRFI 69 ([#174](/tahoma/consent/issues/174)) should follow SRFI 125 ([#178](/tahoma/consent/issues/178)). Chunk 0.18 now stops at the SRFI foundation, testing, and JSON-stress work that the thesis capstone needs nearby; the broad data-library shelves are split out so they can grow coherently: Red Edition data libraries plus their SRFI 45 lazy shim in Chunk 0.20, finalized Tangerine Edition data/numeric/formatting libraries plus the SRFI 146 hash-mapping pair in Chunk 0.21, and the remaining scheduled SRFI utility/rest shelf in Chunk 0.22. Comparator ([#180](/tahoma/consent/issues/180)), the SRFI 16 shim ([#166](/tahoma/consent/issues/166)), SRFI 2 ([#205](/tahoma/consent/issues/205)), SRFI 8 ([#204](/tahoma/consent/issues/204)), SRFI 145 ([#621](/tahoma/consent/issues/621)), SRFI 1 ([#176](/tahoma/consent/issues/176)), SRFI 158 ([#183](/tahoma/consent/issues/183)), the red-black tree helper ([#622](/tahoma/consent/issues/622)), and ordered mappings ([#191](/tahoma/consent/issues/191)) stay in Chunk 0.17 for the ordered SRFI 146 path needed by the memory-model dependency. SRFI 45 ([#170](/tahoma/consent/issues/170)) opens Chunk 0.20 because lazy sequences ([#579](/tahoma/consent/issues/579)) and streams ([#580](/tahoma/consent/issues/580)) explicitly depend on it. SRFI 69 ([#174](/tahoma/consent/issues/174)) stays in Chunk S, and the residual SRFI 13 surface [#464](/tahoma/consent/issues/464) remains in Chunk S because the finalized Red ballot had no string winner; SRFI 152 [#184](/tahoma/consent/issues/184) is only non-docket string substrate for libraries that currently declare it.\n- Host-neutral search ([#267](/tahoma/consent/issues/267)) should follow ~~[#32](/tahoma/consent/issues/32)~~, ~~[#28](/tahoma/consent/issues/28)~~, ~~[#55](/tahoma/consent/issues/55)~~, and [#235](/tahoma/consent/issues/235); it should expose a portable agent-facing search contract while adapting host-specific providers behind the boundary.\n- Agent task lifecycle and control loop design (~~[#281](/tahoma/consent/issues/281)~~) should follow the structured event channel (~~[#21](/tahoma/consent/issues/21)~~), scoped memory (~~[#22](/tahoma/consent/issues/22)~~), capability environment (~~[#102](/tahoma/consent/issues/102)~~), and model provider routing (~~[#26](/tahoma/consent/issues/26)~~) for its design slice, while staying aligned with the later provider capability domain ([#223](/tahoma/consent/issues/223)). It should define how plans (~~[#29](/tahoma/consent/issues/29)~~), rules ([#58](/tahoma/consent/issues/58)), workflow patterns ([#59](/tahoma/consent/issues/59)), skills ([#38](/tahoma/consent/issues/38), [#40](/tahoma/consent/issues/40), [#39](/tahoma/consent/issues/39)), transcripts (~~[#42](/tahoma/consent/issues/42)~~), collaboration UX ([#52](/tahoma/consent/issues/52)), jobs and budgets (~~[#46](/tahoma/consent/issues/46)~~, ~~[#51](/tahoma/consent/issues/51)~~), providers (~~[#26](/tahoma/consent/issues/26)~~, [#223](/tahoma/consent/issues/223)), approvals and grants (~~[#30](/tahoma/consent/issues/30)~~, ~~[#43](/tahoma/consent/issues/43)~~), and host capabilities compose into a running task-oriented agent, and it should prove that composition with at least one remote provider API and one local inference engine/API using shared Scheme-readable request, result, redaction, transcript, budget, cancellation, and audit datums.\n- Task lifecycle records (~~[#285](/tahoma/consent/issues/285)~~) should follow ~~[#281](/tahoma/consent/issues/281)~~, ~~[#21](/tahoma/consent/issues/21)~~, ~~[#22](/tahoma/consent/issues/22)~~, ~~[#29](/tahoma/consent/issues/29)~~, and ~~[#102](/tahoma/consent/issues/102)~~, and should precede the minimal runner (~~[#286](/tahoma/consent/issues/286)~~), control-loop fixtures (~~[#287](/tahoma/consent/issues/287)~~), and task persistence/resume work ([#288](/tahoma/consent/issues/288)).\n- Minimal task runner work (~~[#286](/tahoma/consent/issues/286)~~) should follow ~~[#285](/tahoma/consent/issues/285)~~ plus the plan, approval, grant, job, budget, and capability substrate, and should provide the first executable control-loop slice before production scheduling or provider hardening. ~~[#286](/tahoma/consent/issues/286)~~, the control-loop fixtures (~~[#287](/tahoma/consent/issues/287)~~), and comprehensive budgets (~~[#51](/tahoma/consent/issues/51)~~) are pulled forward into the Chunk 0.17 REPL agent harness; ~~[#286](/tahoma/consent/issues/286)~~'s declared dependencies are all closed except ~~[#51](/tahoma/consent/issues/51)~~, which is why ~~[#51](/tahoma/consent/issues/51)~~ rides forward with it.\n- The Chunk 0.17 REPL agent harness composes already-shipped substrate into REPL verbs and may run on stubbed providers, so it does not require the later provider/streaming/persistence hardening. Scheme-callable session management (~~[#395](/tahoma/consent/issues/395)~~) should follow sessions (~~[#41](/tahoma/consent/issues/41)~~) and the capability environment (~~[#102](/tahoma/consent/issues/102)~~) and reuse the REPL shells (~~[#360](/tahoma/consent/issues/360)~~, ~~[#391](/tahoma/consent/issues/391)~~); the agent abstraction and automatic selection (~~[#396](/tahoma/consent/issues/396)~~) should follow model/role routing (~~[#26](/tahoma/consent/issues/26)~~) and task records (~~[#285](/tahoma/consent/issues/285)~~) and consume rules/skills/workflow ([#58](/tahoma/consent/issues/58), [#38](/tahoma/consent/issues/38), [#40](/tahoma/consent/issues/40), [#59](/tahoma/consent/issues/59)) where available, degrading to a default agent otherwise; the `(agent prompt)` verbs (~~[#397](/tahoma/consent/issues/397)~~) should follow ~~[#396](/tahoma/consent/issues/396)~~, ~~[#395](/tahoma/consent/issues/395)~~, the minimal task runner (~~[#286](/tahoma/consent/issues/286)~~), and budgets (~~[#51](/tahoma/consent/issues/51)~~); the quick-start guide ([#398](/tahoma/consent/issues/398)) should follow the three. Real (non-stub) streaming providers build on the now-promoted JSON translator ([#185](/tahoma/consent/issues/185)) but still reconverge with the provider capability domain ([#223](/tahoma/consent/issues/223)), outward protocols ([#57](/tahoma/consent/issues/57)), and the broader SRFI/SSE substrate ([#54](/tahoma/consent/issues/54)) in the providers chunk.\n- Task control-loop fixtures (~~[#287](/tahoma/consent/issues/287)~~) should follow ~~[#285](/tahoma/consent/issues/285)~~ and ~~[#286](/tahoma/consent/issues/286)~~, then become the shared scenario corpus for task persistence ([#288](/tahoma/consent/issues/288)), provider proof fixtures ([#289](/tahoma/consent/issues/289)), collaboration UX ([#52](/tahoma/consent/issues/52)), and future task-runner conformance. The append-only memory model ([#564](/tahoma/consent/issues/564)) should follow the session single-source pilot ([#439](/tahoma/consent/issues/439)) and memory single-source follow-up ([#437](/tahoma/consent/issues/437)) so it extends the portable-owned memory store rather than the duplicate Emacs twin.\n- Task persistence and resume work ([#288](/tahoma/consent/issues/288)) should follow [#48](/tahoma/consent/issues/48), ~~[#285](/tahoma/consent/issues/285)~~, ~~[#41](/tahoma/consent/issues/41)~~, ~~[#42](/tahoma/consent/issues/42)~~, and ~~[#49](/tahoma/consent/issues/49)~~, and must revalidate authority, redaction, budgets, provider disclosure, and stale handles before a resumed task performs effects.\n- Live provider CI smokes ([#318](/tahoma/consent/issues/318), [#319](/tahoma/consent/issues/319), and [#320](/tahoma/consent/issues/320)) should follow ~~[#26](/tahoma/consent/issues/26)~~ and ~~[#69](/tahoma/consent/issues/69)~~, stay focused on direct local provider routing, transport, and fail-closed behavior, and avoid turning the required live job into a provider matrix or extra model-download path.\n- Remote and local provider proof fixtures ([#289](/tahoma/consent/issues/289)) should follow ~~[#281](/tahoma/consent/issues/281)~~, ~~[#286](/tahoma/consent/issues/286)~~, ~~[#26](/tahoma/consent/issues/26)~~, [#223](/tahoma/consent/issues/223), ~~[#49](/tahoma/consent/issues/49)~~, ~~[#51](/tahoma/consent/issues/51)~~, [#57](/tahoma/consent/issues/57), and ~~[#290](/tahoma/consent/issues/290)~~, and should demonstrate one remote provider API plus one local inference API through the same task lifecycle and provider datums.\n- The live provider control-loop CI proof ([#321](/tahoma/consent/issues/321)) should follow [#289](/tahoma/consent/issues/289) plus the minimal runner, fixture, provider, redaction, budget, protocol, and network substrate (~~[#286](/tahoma/consent/issues/286)~~, ~~[#287](/tahoma/consent/issues/287)~~, ~~[#26](/tahoma/consent/issues/26)~~, ~~[#49](/tahoma/consent/issues/49)~~, ~~[#51](/tahoma/consent/issues/51)~~, [#57](/tahoma/consent/issues/57), ~~[#69](/tahoma/consent/issues/69)~~, [#223](/tahoma/consent/issues/223), and ~~[#290](/tahoma/consent/issues/290)~~), and should prove one tiny live local provider call through task lifecycle records without requiring remote credentials.\n- Host adapter contract conformance ([#237](/tahoma/consent/issues/237)) should follow multi-host boundaries (~~[#55](/tahoma/consent/issues/55)~~), the shared capability environment (~~[#102](/tahoma/consent/issues/102)~~), the shared backend effect path (~~[#103](/tahoma/consent/issues/103)~~), host adapter reflection ([#235](/tahoma/consent/issues/235)), and introspection conformance ([#236](/tahoma/consent/issues/236)); child conformance issues that name native CLI fixtures or process-boundary harnesses should stay after ~~[#229](/tahoma/consent/issues/229)~~ through [#232](/tahoma/consent/issues/232), and future host adapter contract issues should reference [#237](/tahoma/consent/issues/237) for reusable conformance requirements.\n- Native CLI contract work (~~[#136](/tahoma/consent/issues/136)~~) should precede broader host-compiled portable executable packaging (~~[#270](/tahoma/consent/issues/270)~~, ~~[#272](/tahoma/consent/issues/272)~~, and ~~[#273](/tahoma/consent/issues/273)~~), the native CLI harness slices (~~[#229](/tahoma/consent/issues/229)~~ through [#232](/tahoma/consent/issues/232) and ~~[#360](/tahoma/consent/issues/360)~~), and native CLI/daemon VCS adapter work ([#280](/tahoma/consent/issues/280)). The Gambit portable runtime executable (~~[#273](/tahoma/consent/issues/273)~~) should follow the initial `make compile` scaffolding (~~[#270](/tahoma/consent/issues/270)~~) and stay limited to portable R7RS compile/run coverage while the full host-compiled packaging path catches up. Host-compiled executable work remains distinct from the LLIR/native compiler backend ([#115](/tahoma/consent/issues/115) through [#121](/tahoma/consent/issues/121)). The REPL-track slices (~~[#229](/tahoma/consent/issues/229)~~, ~~[#230](/tahoma/consent/issues/230)~~, ~~[#231](/tahoma/consent/issues/231)~~, and ~~[#360](/tahoma/consent/issues/360)~~) are pulled forward into Chunk 0.16 to prioritize a functional REPL, while daemon-control ([#232](/tahoma/consent/issues/232)) and the VCS adapters ([#280](/tahoma/consent/issues/280), [#293](/tahoma/consent/issues/293)) stay in the native CLI/daemon harness chunk; the dependency order below is unchanged because 0.16 precedes that chunk in time.\n- Native CLI daemon manifest fixtures (~~[#229](/tahoma/consent/issues/229)~~) should follow the contract slice (~~[#136](/tahoma/consent/issues/136)~~); mock adapter tests (~~[#230](/tahoma/consent/issues/230)~~) should follow ~~[#229](/tahoma/consent/issues/229)~~; process-boundary (~~[#231](/tahoma/consent/issues/231)~~) should follow ~~[#229](/tahoma/consent/issues/229)~~ and ~~[#230](/tahoma/consent/issues/230)~~; the portable terminal REPL shell (~~[#360](/tahoma/consent/issues/360)~~) should follow ~~[#231](/tahoma/consent/issues/231)~~ and the policy-gated `(scheme repl)` interaction environment (~~[#313](/tahoma/consent/issues/313)~~); daemon-control ([#232](/tahoma/consent/issues/232)) should follow ~~[#229](/tahoma/consent/issues/229)~~ and ~~[#230](/tahoma/consent/issues/230)~~ as a sibling host-boundary validation track.\n- The shared cross-host REPL interaction contract (~~[#390](/tahoma/consent/issues/390)~~) should follow the merged policy-gated `(scheme repl)` interaction environment (~~[#313](/tahoma/consent/issues/313)~~/~~[#314](/tahoma/consent/issues/314)~~) and frame both the portable terminal REPL shell (~~[#360](/tahoma/consent/issues/360)~~) and the Emacs incremental REPL parity entry (~~[#391](/tahoma/consent/issues/391)~~); the shared REPL parity conformance fixtures (~~[#392](/tahoma/consent/issues/392)~~) should follow both host REPL implementations and feed the Emacs-Lisp/portable parity CI gate (~~[#374](/tahoma/consent/issues/374)~~); the REPL documentation (~~[#393](/tahoma/consent/issues/393)~~) should follow the two host implementations.\n- Shebang-style executable script handling (~~[#399](/tahoma/consent/issues/399)~~) is the non-interactive twin of the terminal REPL (~~[#360](/tahoma/consent/issues/360)~~): it extends the existing `--script` path, recognizes a leading shebang narrowly (first-line `#!` followed by `/` or whitespace) at the script-loading boundary so `#!fold-case` and other `#!`-tokens keep their reader meaning, and inherits the batch/cli fail-closed policy posture from the native CLI/daemon adapter contract (~~[#136](/tahoma/consent/issues/136)~~). The promptable-script path — a shebang script calling `(prompt …)` — is owned by ~~[#400](/tahoma/consent/issues/400)~~ in Chunk 0.17 (which extends the ~~[#136](/tahoma/consent/issues/136)~~ batch fail-closed posture to provider/agent grants and depends on the `(agent prompt)` verbs (~~[#397](/tahoma/consent/issues/397)~~) and budgets (~~[#51](/tahoma/consent/issues/51)~~), plus the Emacs incremental REPL parity entry (~~[#391](/tahoma/consent/issues/391)~~) for the Emacs side of its both-host script-execution deliverable), and is out of scope for ~~[#399](/tahoma/consent/issues/399)~~.\n- Native CLI/daemon VCS adapter work ([#280](/tahoma/consent/issues/280)) should follow the native CLI contract (~~[#136](/tahoma/consent/issues/136)~~) and shared VCS contract (~~[#266](/tahoma/consent/issues/266)~~), reuse the portable `(agent vcs)` records and parsers, and keep read-only VCS observation distinct from mutating VCS authority (~~[#279](/tahoma/consent/issues/279)~~).\n- Native CLI/daemon mutating VCS adapter work ([#293](/tahoma/consent/issues/293)) should follow ~~[#279](/tahoma/consent/issues/279)~~, [#280](/tahoma/consent/issues/280), ~~[#136](/tahoma/consent/issues/136)~~, ~~[#222](/tahoma/consent/issues/222)~~, [#244](/tahoma/consent/issues/244), and ~~[#49](/tahoma/consent/issues/49)~~, and prove the same mutating VCS authority boundary outside Emacs.\n- First-class Git metadata/ref library ([#695](/tahoma/consent/issues/695)) should follow the shared VCS contract (~~[#266](/tahoma/consent/issues/266)~~) and shared policy decision datums ([#684](/tahoma/consent/issues/684)), define Git-specific object/ref/notes/trailer records separately from generic `(agent vcs)`, and remain a substrate for repository-owned workflow rather than a hosted-forge API.\n- Repo-owned collaboration metadata and forge-independent workflow ([#696](/tahoma/consent/issues/696)) should follow persistence ([#48](/tahoma/consent/issues/48)), shared VCS records (~~[#266](/tahoma/consent/issues/266)~~), policy decision datums ([#684](/tahoma/consent/issues/684)), and Git metadata ([#695](/tahoma/consent/issues/695)); it should preserve the nuclear replay/hosting/notes/CI/agent-tooling brainstorming record, define canonical repository-owned issue/review/CI/migration records, and inform human collaboration UX ([#52](/tahoma/consent/issues/52)), standard workflow patterns ([#59](/tahoma/consent/issues/59)), dependency-metadata parity ([#446](/tahoma/consent/issues/446)), and CI receipt storage ([#471](/tahoma/consent/issues/471)).\n- Rules ([#58](/tahoma/consent/issues/58)) should remain distinct from policy (~~[#7](/tahoma/consent/issues/7)~~): rules guide behavior, policy gates authority.\n- Comprehensive budgets (~~[#51](/tahoma/consent/issues/51)~~) should consolidate after jobs (~~[#46](/tahoma/consent/issues/46)~~) and model provider routing (~~[#26](/tahoma/consent/issues/26)~~), while ~~[#3](/tahoma/consent/issues/3)~~ supplies the earliest runaway-eval guardrails.\n- Budget ledger and stop receipt work ([#291](/tahoma/consent/issues/291)) should follow ~~[#51](/tahoma/consent/issues/51)~~, ~~[#21](/tahoma/consent/issues/21)~~, ~~[#46](/tahoma/consent/issues/46)~~, and ~~[#102](/tahoma/consent/issues/102)~~ so tasks, jobs, transcripts, providers, and host capabilities can explain budget exhaustion through one inspectable record.\n- Outward protocol libraries ([#57](/tahoma/consent/issues/57)) should follow MCP exposure ([#9](/tahoma/consent/issues/9)), model/provider routing (~~[#26](/tahoma/consent/issues/26)~~), Hugging Face bootstrap profiles ([#25](/tahoma/consent/issues/25)), package resolution ([#50](/tahoma/consent/issues/50)), and vendored SRFI bundle tracking ([#54](/tahoma/consent/issues/54)).\n- External protocol exposure ([#9](/tahoma/consent/issues/9)) should wait until local eval, policy, session UX, and `agent-yield` are coherent.\n- JVM IDE platform contracts ([#151](/tahoma/consent/issues/151)) should follow the lighter editor/protocol contracts ([#140](/tahoma/consent/issues/140) and [#147](/tahoma/consent/issues/147)) and WASI component imports ([#149](/tahoma/consent/issues/149)).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The issue dependency graph has no obvious foundational cycles.\n- Vague dependency placeholders are replaced with explicit issue numbers when possible.\n- The numbered chunk map remains flat, time ordered, and chunk-sized rather than nested by umbrella topic; milestone bands may annotate contiguous chunks but must not nest issues, and the lettered draw-from pools (S, H, C) hold unscheduled work without version positions.\n- Umbrella issues are identified in a separate section from the chunk map.\n- Every open repository issue is referenced somewhere in this roadmap issue; completed work is recorded in `docs/release-notes.md`.\n- New design topics can be slotted into this roadmap without reshuffling the whole backlog.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nDepends on ~~[#1](/tahoma/consent/issues/1)~~.\n\n## Notes\n\nThis is a map, not a prison. It should keep the backlog legible while still letting us build thin vertical slices when that teaches us more.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tahoma/consent/issues/53/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tahoma/consent/issues/53/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/398","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/398/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/398/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/398/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/398","id":3974807149,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa87s6r5t","number":398,"title":"[QUEST] Harden the Chain — Security Quest, 67 RTC Total","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10115035859,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"RTC-paid bounty"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":65,"created_at":"2026-02-22T15:25:06Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T19:04:22Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Quest Chain: Harden the Chain\n\nFor security-minded contributors. Complete each step to earn up to **100 RTC** and the **Guardian** title.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Read the Architecture (10 RTC)\nRead the codebase and write a 500+ word security assessment covering:\n- How attestation works (the \\`/attest/submit\\` flow)\n- How hardware fingerprinting prevents VM farms\n- How epoch rewards are calculated and distributed\n- One potential attack vector you identified\n\n**Prove it:** Post your assessment as a comment or gist link.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Reproduce a Known Fix (15 RTC)\nPick one vulnerability from BuilderFred's audit (all 6 are fixed):\n1. VM Fingerprint Bypass\n2. Antiquity Spoofing\n3. Mock Signature Mode\n4. Inline PubKey Hijack\n5. SQL Schema Mismatch\n6. Hardware Binding Bypass\n\nSet up a local test environment and demonstrate you understand HOW the fix works by:\n- Describing the attack before the fix\n- Showing the fix in the code\n- Explaining why the fix is sufficient (or isn't)\n\n**Prove it:** Write-up with code references.\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Find Something New (75 RTC)\nFind and report a previously unknown security issue. Must include:\n- Clear description of the vulnerability\n- Steps to reproduce\n- Severity assessment (Critical/High/Medium/Low)\n- Suggested fix\n\n**Prove it:** File a responsible disclosure via the SECURITY.md process. If confirmed, earn the full 75 RTC + Guardian title.\n\n---\n\n### Completion\n\n| Steps | Reward | Title |\n|-------|--------|-------|\n| Step 1 only | 10 RTC | Security Explorer |\n| Steps 1 + 2 | 25 RTC | Security Analyst |\n| Steps 1 + 2 + 3 | **100 RTC** | **Guardian** |\n\n*You don't have to find a new vulnerability to earn from Steps 1 and 2. Those reward understanding, not just discovery.*","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/398/reactions","total_count":6,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":1,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/398/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ANAVHEOBA/PrivacyLayer/issues/349","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ANAVHEOBA/PrivacyLayer","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ANAVHEOBA/PrivacyLayer/issues/349/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ANAVHEOBA/PrivacyLayer/issues/349/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ANAVHEOBA/PrivacyLayer/issues/349/events","html_url":"https://github.com/ANAVHEOBA/PrivacyLayer/issues/349","id":4331675091,"node_id":"I_kwDORsVGvc8AAAABAjAd0w","number":349,"title":"ZK-073: Redesign relayer binding and zero-relayer semantics across SDK and contract code","user":{"login":"ANAVHEOBA","id":116527512,"node_id":"U_kgDOBvIRmA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116527512?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ANAVHEOBA","html_url":"https://github.com/ANAVHEOBA","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ANAVHEOBA/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ANAVHEOBA/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ANAVHEOBA/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ANAVHEOBA/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ANAVHEOBA/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ANAVHEOBA/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ANAVHEOBA/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ANAVHEOBA/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ANAVHEOBA/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10478863820,"node_id":"LA_kwDORsVGvc8AAAACcJbFzA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ANAVHEOBA/PrivacyLayer/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"7057FF","default":false,"description":"Eligible for Drips Wave bounty review"},{"id":10478866637,"node_id":"LA_kwDORsVGvc8AAAACcJbQzQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ANAVHEOBA/PrivacyLayer/labels/circuits","name":"circuits","color":"0052CC","default":false,"description":"Noir circuit and proving work"},{"id":10478867665,"node_id":"LA_kwDORsVGvc8AAAACcJbU0Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ANAVHEOBA/PrivacyLayer/labels/testing","name":"testing","color":"5319E7","default":false,"description":"Coverage, fixtures, fuzzing, and regression work"},{"id":10478867848,"node_id":"LA_kwDORsVGvc8AAAACcJbViA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ANAVHEOBA/PrivacyLayer/labels/security","name":"security","color":"B60205","default":false,"description":"Security review, audit prep, and hardening work"},{"id":10478868608,"node_id":"LA_kwDORsVGvc8AAAACcJbYgA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ANAVHEOBA/PrivacyLayer/labels/priority:%20high","name":"priority: high","color":"B60205","default":false,"description":"Critical path work for the current wave"},{"id":10771568426,"node_id":"LA_kwDORsVGvc8AAAACggkXKg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ANAVHEOBA/PrivacyLayer/labels/complexity:%20high","name":"complexity: high","color":"B60205","default":false,"description":"Drips complexity: high / 200 points"},{"id":10771569164,"node_id":"LA_kwDORsVGvc8AAAACggkaDA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ANAVHEOBA/PrivacyLayer/labels/area:%20withdraw","name":"area: withdraw","color":"BFDADC","default":false,"description":"Withdrawal circuit constraints and proof semantics"},{"id":10795450195,"node_id":"LA_kwDORsVGvc8AAAACg3V_Uw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ANAVHEOBA/PrivacyLayer/labels/wave:%20zk-2","name":"wave: zk-2","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"Wave 2: ZK parity, backend, and deployment hardening"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"soomtochukwu","id":142386413,"node_id":"U_kgDOCHyk7Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/142386413?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/soomtochukwu","html_url":"https://github.com/soomtochukwu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soomtochukwu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soomtochukwu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soomtochukwu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soomtochukwu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soomtochukwu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soomtochukwu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soomtochukwu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soomtochukwu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soomtochukwu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":13,"created_at":"2026-04-26T18:45:56Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T18:14:55Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"soomtochukwu","id":142386413,"node_id":"U_kgDOCHyk7Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/142386413?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/soomtochukwu","html_url":"https://github.com/soomtochukwu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soomtochukwu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soomtochukwu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soomtochukwu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soomtochukwu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soomtochukwu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soomtochukwu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soomtochukwu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soomtochukwu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soomtochukwu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Wave: PrivacyLayer ZK Wave 2\nIssue Key: ZK-073\nArea: withdraw\nPriority: High\nDrips Complexity: High\n## Summary\nRecipient binding is not the only mismatch. Relayer handling still mixes zero-field sentinels, decoded addresses, and fee rules in ways that are easy to misapply across stacks.\n## Relevant Code\n- sdk/src/encoding.ts\n- sdk/src/proof.ts\n- circuits/withdraw/src/spend.nr\n- contracts/privacy_pool/src/core/withdraw.rs\n- contracts/privacy_pool/src/utils/address_decoder.rs\n- contracts/privacy_pool/src/utils/validation.rs\n\n## Scope\n- Define one relayer binding contract for no-relayer, relayer-with-fee, and malformed-relayer cases.\n- Align SDK serialization, circuit validation, and Soroban withdraw handling around that contract.\n- Cover fee zero, relayer zero, and relayer mismatch cases in end-to-end tests.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- Relayer handling no longer depends on ad hoc zero-address assumptions in multiple modules.\n- The contract accepts only relayer encodings that the SDK can produce canonically.\n- Regression tests distinguish absent relayer from malformed relayer cleanly.\n\n## Out of Scope\n- New wallet UX and non-ZK frontend polish\n- Unrelated Soroban business logic outside the withdrawal proof boundary\n\n## Dependencies\n- ZK-036\n- ZK-072\n\n## Validation\n- Inspect derived checks: `node scripts/zk_ticket_check.mjs --issue-key ZK-073`\n- Run derived checks: `node scripts/zk_ticket_check.mjs --issue-key ZK-073 --run`\n- Pull requests should include `Wave Issue Key: ZK-073` in the title or body.\n\n## References\n- sdk/src/encoding.ts\n- sdk/src/proof.ts\n- circuits/withdraw/src/spend.nr\n- contracts/privacy_pool/src/core/withdraw.rs\n- contracts/privacy_pool/src/utils/address_decoder.rs\n- contracts/privacy_pool/src/utils/validation.rs\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ANAVHEOBA/PrivacyLayer/issues/349/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ANAVHEOBA/PrivacyLayer/issues/349/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nexussyn/ai-growth-engine/issues/4","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nexussyn/ai-growth-engine","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nexussyn/ai-growth-engine/issues/4/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nexussyn/ai-growth-engine/issues/4/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nexussyn/ai-growth-engine/issues/4/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Nexussyn/ai-growth-engine/issues/4","id":4804271831,"node_id":"I_kwDOTMrmLs8AAAABHlte1w","number":4,"title":"[AGENT-TASK] Mobile-first landing page with wallet deep-link — +15% conversion","user":{"login":"Nexussyn","id":210243486,"node_id":"U_kgDODIgPng","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/210243486?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexussyn","html_url":"https://github.com/Nexussyn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexussyn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexussyn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexussyn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexussyn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexussyn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexussyn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexussyn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexussyn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nexussyn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11409394811,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTMrmLs8AAAACqA2Mew","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nexussyn/ai-growth-engine/labels/good%20first%20issue","name":"good first issue","color":"7057ff","default":true,"description":"Good for newcomers"},{"id":11409407271,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTMrmLs8AAAACqA29Jw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nexussyn/ai-growth-engine/labels/agent-task","name":"agent-task","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":11409407273,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTMrmLs8AAAACqA29KQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nexussyn/ai-growth-engine/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":11409432664,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTMrmLs8AAAACqA4gWA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nexussyn/ai-growth-engine/labels/frontend","name":"frontend","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":19,"created_at":"2026-07-03T14:32:41Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T18:14:30Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## 🎯 Objective\nCreate a mobile-optimized landing page that detects mobile context and shows a simplified CTA with wallet app deep-links.\n\n## 📋 Scope\nThe current landing page is desktop-first. On mobile:\n1. Detect user agent / screen size\n2. Show simplified hero: 1 headline + 1 CTA button\n3. CTA deep-links to MetaMask Mobile, Coinbase Wallet, Rainbow\n4. Track mobile vs desktop conversion separately\n\n## ✅ Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] HTML/CSS/JS mobile landing page (or React component)\n- [ ] User agent detection for mobile\n- [ ] Deep-links for: MetaMask (`metamask://`), Coinbase Wallet (`cbwallet://`), Rainbow (`rainbow://`)\n- [ ] Conversion event tracked in `system_events` with `mobile_landing_cta_click`\n- [ ] Passes Lighthouse mobile score > 90\n- [ ] Works on iOS Safari and Android Chrome\n\n## 📤 Expected Output\n- `src/landing/mobile.html` or `src/components/MobileLanding.tsx`\n- Screenshot/demo in PR description\n\n## 💰 Reward\n`$10 USDC` logged on merge\n\n## 🔗 Context\n- Source: `improvement_proposals.prop_mobile_landing`\n- ~60% of web3 users are on mobile\n- Expected impact: +15% conversion\n\n## 🤖 For AI agents\nBranch: `agent/[your-name]/issue-4`","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nexussyn/ai-growth-engine/issues/4/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nexussyn/ai-growth-engine/issues/4/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ziztigr288c/zap/issues/1","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ziztigr288c/zap","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ziztigr288c/zap/issues/1/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ziztigr288c/zap/issues/1/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ziztigr288c/zap/issues/1/events","html_url":"https://github.com/ziztigr288c/zap/issues/1","id":4820276442,"node_id":"I_kwDOTPVkB88AAAABH0-U2g","number":1,"title":"🎯 Fix incorrect caller information when chaining `WithOptions(zap.AddCallerSkip(...))` multiple times","user":{"login":"ziztigr288c","id":300496999,"node_id":"U_kgDOEek4Zw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/300496999?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ziztigr288c","html_url":"https://github.com/ziztigr288c","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ziztigr288c/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ziztigr288c/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ziztigr288c/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ziztigr288c/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ziztigr288c/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ziztigr288c/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ziztigr288c/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ziztigr288c/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ziztigr288c/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11434917969,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTPVkB88AAAACqZMAUQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ziztigr288c/zap/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":11434917970,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTPVkB88AAAACqZMAUg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ziztigr288c/zap/labels/opire","name":"opire","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":11434917974,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTPVkB88AAAACqZMAVg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ziztigr288c/zap/labels/$10","name":"$10","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":7,"created_at":"2026-07-06T14:50:15Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T18:08:44Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## 📝 Description\nWhen wrapping the Zap logger in multiple layers of helper functions or middleware, developers often chain `.WithOptions(zap.AddCallerSkip(n))` to adjust the stack frame depth so that the correct file and line number are logged. \n\nCurrently, chaining multiple `WithOptions(zap.AddCallerSkip(...))` calls results in incorrect caller information. The caller skip count is not accumulating additively across sequential `WithOptions` calls (for example, calling `.WithOptions(zap.AddCallerSkip(1))` followed by another `.WithOptions(zap.AddCallerSkip(1))` does not correctly skip 2 frames, often resetting or overwriting the skip depth instead).\n\n## 🎯 Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Chaining multiple `WithOptions(zap.AddCallerSkip(d))` calls must be additive (e.g., `logger.WithOptions(zap.AddCallerSkip(1)).WithOptions(zap.AddCallerSkip(2))` must result in a total caller skip of `3`).\n- [ ] The logged caller file, function, and line number must accurately reflect the frame at the resolved cumulative depth.\n- [ ] Existing single-use cases of `zap.AddCallerSkip` must continue to function without breaking.\n- [ ] No performance regressions in the logging hot path when caller tracking is enabled.\n\n## 🛠️ Technical Specifications & Context\nIn `ziztigr288c/zap`, the `Logger` struct and its options are defined across `logger.go` and `options.go`.\n\n1. **`options.go`**:\n   - Locate the `AddCallerSkip(skip int)` option implementation.\n   - Verify if the option is overwriting the caller skip value (e.g., `log.callerSkip = skip`) instead of accumulating it (e.g., `log.callerSkip += skip`).\n   \n2. **`logger.go`**:\n   - Inspect `WithOptions(opts ...Option)` and how it clones the logger.\n   - Ensure that `Logger.clone()` correctly copies the accumulated `callerSkip` value to the cloned instance so that subsequent option applications build upon the copied value.\n   - Check the caller recovery logic (likely using `runtime.Caller` or `runtime.Callers`) to ensure it uses the accumulated `callerSkip` offset correctly.\n\n## 🧪 Verification & Testing\nHunter can verify the fix by adding a test case in `logger_test.go` (or a new test file `caller_test.go`):\n\n```go\nfunc TestChainedCallerSkip(t *testing.T) {\n    observedLogs, logs := observer.New(zap.InfoLevel)\n    \n    // Base logger with caller enabled\n    logger := zap.New(logs, zap.AddCaller())\n\n    // Helper function simulating two layers of wrapping\n    wrapper := func(l *zap.Logger) {\n        // First skip layer\n        l1 := l.WithOptions(zap.AddCallerSkip(1))\n        \n        // Second skip layer (chained)\n        l2 := l1.WithOptions(zap.AddCallerSkip(1))\n        \n        l2.Info(\"test message\")\n    }\n\n    wrapper(logger)\n\n    // Assertions\n    require.Equal(t, 1, observedLogs.Len(), \"Expected exactly one log entry\")\n    logEntry := observedLogs.All()[0]\n    \n    // The caller should point to the line where `wrapper(logger)` was called,\n    // not inside the wrapper or l2.Info call.\n    require.True(t, logEntry.Caller.Defined, \"Caller should be defined\")\n    assert.Contains(t, logEntry.Caller.File, \"logger_test.go\", \"Caller file should be the test file\")\n    assert.Equal(t, 18, logEntry.Caller.Line, \"Caller line should match the wrapper invocation line\") // Adjust line number dynamically in test\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n[![Opire Bounty](https://img.shields.io/badge/bounty-Opire-emerald?style=for-the-badge)](https://github.com/ziztigr288c/zap)\n<br/>\n<hr/>\n\n<details><summary>This repo is using Opire - what does it mean? 👇</summary><br/>💵 Everyone can add rewards for this issue commenting <code>/reward 100</code> (replace <code>100</code> with the amount).<br/>🕵️‍♂️ If someone starts working on this issue to earn the rewards, they can comment <code>/try</code> to let everyone know!<br/>🙌 And when they open the PR, they can comment <code>/claim #1</code> either in the PR description or in a PR's comment.<br/><br/>🪙 Also, everyone can tip any user commenting <code>/tip 20 @ziztigr288c</code> (replace <code>20</code> with the amount, and <code>@ziztigr288c</code> with the user to tip).<br/><br/>📖 If you want to learn more, check out our <a href=\"https://docs.opire.dev\">documentation</a>.</details>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ziztigr288c/zap/issues/1/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ziztigr288c/zap/issues/1/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/APN-Network/bugs/issues/60","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/APN-Network/bugs","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/APN-Network/bugs/issues/60/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/APN-Network/bugs/issues/60/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/APN-Network/bugs/issues/60/events","html_url":"https://github.com/APN-Network/bugs/issues/60","id":4683538166,"node_id":"I_kwDOSv2S3M8AAAABFyke9g","number":60,"title":"README не определяет критерии серьёзности, на которые ссылается раздел «Награды»","user":{"login":"PatGlo1232","id":225620270,"node_id":"U_kgDODXKxLg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225620270?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatGlo1232","html_url":"https://github.com/PatGlo1232","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatGlo1232/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatGlo1232/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatGlo1232/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatGlo1232/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatGlo1232/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatGlo1232/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatGlo1232/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatGlo1232/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatGlo1232/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11130327593,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSv2S3M8AAAACl2tSKQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/APN-Network/bugs/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working"},{"id":11133347081,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSv2S3M8AAAACl5llCQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/APN-Network/bugs/labels/$10","name":"$10","color":"505805","default":false,"description":"Minor UI glitches, wrong labels, or cosmetic issues with a clear reproduction path"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"davvd","id":6305016,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzMDUwMTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6305016?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davvd","html_url":"https://github.com/davvd","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davvd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davvd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davvd/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davvd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davvd/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davvd/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davvd/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davvd/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davvd/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-06-17T13:07:52Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T18:04:30Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"davvd","id":6305016,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzMDUwMTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6305016?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davvd","html_url":"https://github.com/davvd","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davvd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davvd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davvd/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davvd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davvd/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davvd/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davvd/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davvd/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davvd/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"В строке 49 README.md сказано: «We pay $10, $25, or $50 for every accepted bug, depending on its severity» — мы платим $10, $25 или $50 за каждый принятый баг в зависимости от его серьёзности. Однако нигде в файле не объясняется, что именно означает «серьёзность» и чем отличаются три уровня выплат.\n\nВ CONTRIBUTING.md есть полная таблица в разделе «Reward Tiers», которая связывает серьёзность с суммой:\n- $10 — мелкие ошибки интерфейса, неправильные подписи или косметические недочёты\n- $25 — функциональные баги основных функций: подключение, переключение серверов, подписки, переподключение\n- $50 — критические баги, затрагивающие безопасность или приватность: утечки трафика, сбои килл-свитча, потеря данных\n\nПоскольку README — это первое, что видит большинство репортёров, читатель не имеет возможности определить, к какому уровню относится его баг. Добавление краткого описания критериев серьёзности (или ссылки на CONTRIBUTING.md) устранит этот пробел.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/APN-Network/bugs/issues/60/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/APN-Network/bugs/issues/60/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/66","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/66/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/66/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/66/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/66","id":3904273917,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa87otn39","number":66,"title":"[BOUNTY] 🔴 Red Team: x402 Payment Protocol Exploits (100 RTC)","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10115035859,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"RTC-paid bounty"},{"id":10115035877,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy5Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/open","name":"open","color":"1D76DB","default":false,"description":"Open for claims"},{"id":10119173301,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWyZUtQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/red-team","name":"red-team","color":"D93F0B","default":false,"description":"Adversarial security testing"},{"id":10119173491,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWyZVcw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/hardening","name":"hardening","color":"0052CC","default":false,"description":"Security improvements"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":88,"created_at":"2026-02-06T01:03:30Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T17:51:30Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Red Team Bounty: x402 Payment Protocol Exploits\n\n**Reward: 100 RTC** (~$10 at reference rate)\n\n### Target\nThe x402/8004 HTTP Payment Protocol implementation merged in Rustchain PR #5 by @erdogan98.\n\n**Code location:** `x402/` directory in Rustchain repo\n\n### What to Attack\n\n1. **Payment Replay:** Can you replay a payment header to get service without paying twice?\n2. **Amount Manipulation:** Can you modify payment amount after signing?\n3. **Receipt Forgery:** Can you forge a valid payment receipt?\n4. **Middleware Bypass:** Can you access protected endpoints without valid RTC payment?\n5. **Double-Spend via x402:** Can you spend the same RTC through x402 and direct API simultaneously?\n6. **Client Impersonation:** Can you use someone else's payment credentials?\n\n### Rules\n- Document each vulnerability with reproduction steps\n- Classify severity (Critical/High/Medium/Low)\n- Suggest fix for each finding\n- Do NOT exploit against production — test locally or on a test node\n- Responsible disclosure: report here first, don't publicize until fixed\n\n### Payout Scale\n| Severity | Bonus |\n|----------|-------|\n| Critical (fund drain) | +100 RTC |\n| High (auth bypass) | +50 RTC |\n| Medium (info leak) | +25 RTC |\n| Low (edge case) | Base 100 RTC |\n\n### Deliverables\n- Security report with PoC for each finding\n- Suggested fixes\n- PR with patches (bonus RTC)\n\n### Claiming\nComment with your security testing background.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/66/reactions","total_count":9,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":2,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/66/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/58","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/58/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/58/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/58/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/58","id":3893861852,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa87oF53c","number":58,"title":"[BOUNTY] 🔴 Red Team: Cross-Node Consensus Attacks (100 RTC)","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10115035859,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"RTC-paid bounty"},{"id":10115035877,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy5Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/open","name":"open","color":"1D76DB","default":false,"description":"Open for claims"},{"id":10119173301,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWyZUtQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/red-team","name":"red-team","color":"D93F0B","default":false,"description":"Adversarial security testing"},{"id":10119173491,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWyZVcw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/hardening","name":"hardening","color":"0052CC","default":false,"description":"Security improvements"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":97,"created_at":"2026-02-04T00:20:49Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T17:50:30Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## 🔴 Red Team Bounty — Consensus & Replication Attacks\n\n**Bounty: 200 RTC (~$20)**\n\n### Target\n\nRustChain runs 3 attestation nodes that should maintain consensus. Can you break it?\n\n### Attack Vectors to Test\n\n1. **Split Brain** — Can you make nodes disagree on balances/state?\n2. **Replay Across Nodes** — Replay valid attestation to different node?\n3. **Database Desync** — Force nodes out of sync?\n4. **Eclipse Attack** — Isolate a node and feed it false data?\n5. **Time Manipulation** — Exploit clock differences between nodes?\n\n### Node Addresses\n\n```\nNode 1: 50.28.86.131 (Primary)\nNode 2: 50.28.86.153 (Ergo Anchor)\nNode 3: 76.8.228.245:8099 (External)\n```\n\n### Deliverable\n\n- Attack methodology\n- Evidence of consensus break (screenshots, logs)\n- Impact assessment\n- Recommended mitigations\n\n### Rules\n\n- Do NOT permanently damage node state\n- Responsible disclosure\n- Document everything\n\n**200 RTC** for valid consensus attacks. Critical findings may earn bonus.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/58/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/58/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/397","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/397/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/397/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/397/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/397","id":3974806452,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa87s6ru0","number":397,"title":"[QUEST] Become a RustChain Miner — 5 Steps, 50 RTC Total","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10115035859,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"RTC-paid bounty"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":16,"created_at":"2026-02-22T15:24:52Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T17:45:42Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Quest Chain: Become a RustChain Miner\n\nComplete each step in order. Each step unlocks the next. **50 RTC total** for completing the full chain.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Install and Run (5 RTC)\n\\`\\`\\`bash\npip install clawrtc\nclawrtc mine --wallet YOUR_NAME --dry-run\n\\`\\`\\`\n**Prove it:** Screenshot or paste your \\`--dry-run\\` output showing your hardware fingerprint.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Mine Your First Block (10 RTC)\n\\`\\`\\`bash\nclawrtc mine --wallet YOUR_NAME\n\\`\\`\\`\nRun the miner for at least 1 hour on real hardware (not a VM — our fingerprinting will detect it).\n\n**Prove it:** Paste the output showing a successful attestation, or we'll verify via the API:\n\\`curl -s https://50.28.86.131/api/miners | python3 -m json.tool\\`\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Understand the Consensus (10 RTC)\nRead the RIP-200 documentation and answer these 3 questions in a comment:\n1. Why does a PowerPC G4 earn more RTC than a modern x86 CPU?\n2. What are the 6 hardware fingerprint checks that prevent VM farming?\n3. What is the current epoch reward pot and how is it distributed?\n\n**No copying from docs** — explain in your own words. We can tell.\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Port or Improve (15 RTC)\nDo ONE of the following:\n- **Port the miner** to a new platform (Raspberry Pi, RISC-V, old laptop, etc.) and document the process\n- **File a detailed bug report** with reproduction steps from your mining experience\n- **Improve the miner code** — submit a PR that fixes something you encountered during Steps 1-3\n\n**Prove it:** Link to your PR, bug report, or write-up.\n\n---\n\n### Step 5: Teach Someone Else (10 RTC)\nWrite a tutorial, blog post, or video showing someone else how to mine RustChain. Publish it on Dev.to, Medium, YouTube, or your personal blog.\n\n**Prove it:** Link to your published content. Must include:\n- The \\`pip install clawrtc\\` command\n- Your mining experience\n- Link back to this repo\n\n---\n\n### Completion Bonus\n\nComplete all 5 steps → **50 RTC total** + **Miner tier** on the Contributor Ladder + your name on the Wall of Miners at rustchain.org.\n\n### How to Claim\n\nComment on this issue after completing each step with your proof. We verify and pay per step. You don't have to complete all 5 at once — take your time.\n\n\\`\\`\\`\nStep completed: 1\nProof: [screenshot/link/paste]\nRTC wallet: YOUR_WALLET_NAME\n\\`\\`\\`\n\n---\n\n*Quest chains require real effort and understanding. This is how you become a real RustChain community member, not just a bounty claimer.*","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/397/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/397/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/520","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/520/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/520/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/520/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/520","id":4006215511,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa87uyf9X","number":520,"title":"[Achievement] Bug Hunter - Find a Real Bug - 2 RTC","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10115035859,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"RTC-paid bounty"},{"id":10115035877,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy5Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/open","name":"open","color":"1D76DB","default":false,"description":"Open for claims"},{"id":10115035923,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWuczEw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/standard","name":"standard","color":"D4C5F9","default":false,"description":"10-50 RTC"},{"id":10153071106,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACXSuSAg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/community","name":"community","color":"5319E7","default":false,"description":"Community engagement"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":127,"created_at":"2026-03-01T04:13:51Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T17:25:40Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Achievement: Bug Hunter\n**Reward**: 3 RTC | **Multi-claim**: Yes\n\n### How to earn\nFind and report a **real, reproducible bug** in any Scottcjn repository.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Bug is real and reproducible\n- [ ] Filed as a proper issue with steps to reproduce\n- [ ] Not a duplicate of an existing issue\n- [ ] Includes environment info (OS, version, etc.)\n\n### How to claim\nFile a bug issue, then comment here with the link. 3 RTC if confirmed valid.\n\n**Reward**: 3 RTC (~$0.30) | **Multi-claim**","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/520/reactions","total_count":7,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":1,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/520/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/StableRoute-Org/Stableroute-frontend/issues/71","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/StableRoute-Org/Stableroute-frontend","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/StableRoute-Org/Stableroute-frontend/issues/71/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/StableRoute-Org/Stableroute-frontend/issues/71/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/StableRoute-Org/Stableroute-frontend/issues/71/events","html_url":"https://github.com/StableRoute-Org/Stableroute-frontend/issues/71","id":4724269470,"node_id":"I_kwDORndync8AAAABGZahng","number":71,"title":"Add issue and pull-request templates with a contributor and a11y checklist","user":{"login":"mikewheeleer","id":268014356,"node_id":"U_kgDOD_mTFA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/268014356?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikewheeleer","html_url":"https://github.com/mikewheeleer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikewheeleer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikewheeleer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikewheeleer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikewheeleer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikewheeleer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikewheeleer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikewheeleer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikewheeleer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikewheeleer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11271928644,"node_id":"LA_kwDORndync8AAAACn9v7RA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/StableRoute-Org/Stableroute-frontend/labels/GRANTFOX%20OSS","name":"GRANTFOX OSS","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"GrantFox open-source campaign task"},{"id":11271928722,"node_id":"LA_kwDORndync8AAAACn9v7kg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/StableRoute-Org/Stableroute-frontend/labels/MAYBE%20REWARDED","name":"MAYBE REWARDED","color":"FBCA04","default":false,"description":"May be rewarded under the GrantFox campaign"},{"id":11271928817,"node_id":"LA_kwDORndync8AAAACn9v78Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/StableRoute-Org/Stableroute-frontend/labels/OFFICIAL%20CAMPAIGN","name":"OFFICIAL CAMPAIGN","color":"8E44AD","default":false,"description":"Official GrantFox campaign issue"},{"id":11271931163,"node_id":"LA_kwDORndync8AAAACn9wFGw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/StableRoute-Org/Stableroute-frontend/labels/priority:low","name":"priority:low","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"Low priority"},{"id":11271931382,"node_id":"LA_kwDORndync8AAAACn9wF9g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/StableRoute-Org/Stableroute-frontend/labels/stack:nextjs","name":"stack:nextjs","color":"0A0A0A","default":false,"description":"Next.js"},{"id":11271931492,"node_id":"LA_kwDORndync8AAAACn9wGZA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/StableRoute-Org/Stableroute-frontend/labels/stack:react","name":"stack:react","color":"61DAFB","default":false,"description":"React"},{"id":11271931576,"node_id":"LA_kwDORndync8AAAACn9wGuA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/StableRoute-Org/Stableroute-frontend/labels/stack:typescript","name":"stack:typescript","color":"3178C6","default":false,"description":"TypeScript"},{"id":11271931712,"node_id":"LA_kwDORndync8AAAACn9wHQA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/StableRoute-Org/Stableroute-frontend/labels/type:docs","name":"type:docs","color":"5319E7","default":false,"description":"Documentation"},{"id":11312497689,"node_id":"LA_kwDORndync8AAAACokcEGQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/StableRoute-Org/Stableroute-frontend/labels/area:github","name":"area:github","color":"7D3C98","default":false,"description":"github"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-06-23T09:03:10Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T17:15:18Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":{"id":31873878,"node_id":"IT_kwDOD_5V184B5ltW","name":"Feature","description":"A request, idea, or new functionality","color":"blue","created_at":"2026-03-15T08:20:12Z","updated_at":"2026-03-15T08:20:12Z","is_enabled":true},"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<!-- ghit#filepath: /Users/jagadeesh/mike/driops/stableroute/Stableroute-frontend -->\n\n## Add GitHub issue and PR templates for the repository\n\n### Description\nThe repo has a CI workflow at [`.github/workflows/ci.yml`](.github/workflows/ci.yml) but no `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE` and no `PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`, so contributors to this campaign have no standard structure for reporting bugs/requesting features or for opening a merge-ready PR. This issue adds those templates, aligned with the project's test/lint/build conventions.\n\n### Requirements and context\n- **Repository scope:** StableRoute-Org/Stableroute-frontend only.\n- Add `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/bug_report.md` and `feature_request.md` (or the YAML `*.yml` forms) capturing reproduction, expected behaviour, affected route/component, and environment.\n- Add `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md` with a checklist mirroring the campaign expectations: tests added, `npm run lint`/`npm test`/`npm run build` green, docs updated, and accessibility considered.\n- Reference the branch-naming convention (`type/area-slug`) used across these issues and link to the Discord.\n- Keep the templates concise and Markdown-valid; do not alter the CI workflow.\n\n### Suggested execution\n- Fork the repo and create a branch\n- `git checkout -b docs/github-25-templates`\n- Implement changes\n  - **Write code in:** n/a (docs) — add files under `.github/`.\n  - **Write comprehensive tests in:** n/a — verify the templates render on GitHub and reference real scripts in [`package.json`](package.json).\n  - **Add documentation:** link the templates from the Contributing section of [`README.md`](README.md).\n  - Ensure referenced commands and branch convention match the repo.\n  - Validate Markdown/YAML correctness.\n- Test and commit\n\n### Test and commit\n- Run `npm run lint` and `npm run build` to confirm nothing else is affected.\n- Cover edge cases: bug and feature templates present, PR checklist accurate, and links resolve.\n- Include a rendered preview note in the PR description.\n\n### Example commit message\n`docs: add issue and pull-request templates with contributor checklist`\n\n### Guidelines\n- **Minimum 95 percent test coverage** for impacted modules.\n- Clear, reviewer-focused documentation.\n- **Timeframe: 96 hours.**\n\n### Community & contribution rewards\n- 💬 **Join the StableRoute community on Discord for questions, reviews, and faster merges:** https://discord.gg/37aCpusvx\n- ⭐ This is a **GrantFox OSS / Official Campaign** task and **may be rewarded**. When your PR is merged you'll be prompted to rate the project — if this issue and the maintainers helped you ship, we'd be grateful for a **5-star rating**. Clear questions in Discord and tidy, well-tested PRs are the fastest path to a merge and a reward.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/StableRoute-Org/Stableroute-frontend/issues/71/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/StableRoute-Org/Stableroute-frontend/issues/71/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claudes-world/blog-claude-do/issues/1","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claudes-world/blog-claude-do","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claudes-world/blog-claude-do/issues/1/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claudes-world/blog-claude-do/issues/1/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claudes-world/blog-claude-do/issues/1/events","html_url":"https://github.com/claudes-world/blog-claude-do/issues/1","id":3160902810,"node_id":"I_kwDOO-h3tc68Z4ya","number":1,"title":"Agent Research for Agent-Managed Blog and Social Platform","user":{"login":"mcorrig4","id":1342367,"node_id":"MDQ