ents{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Duhneekuh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-07-06T14:10:18Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T15:27:01Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"alexgbo","id":179588022,"node_id":"U_kgDOCrRLtg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/179588022?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgbo","html_url":"https://github.com/alexgbo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgbo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgbo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgbo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgbo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgbo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgbo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgbo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgbo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgbo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Terms and Conditions\n\n- [x] I agree to the [Grant Agreement](https://9ba4718c-5c73-47c3-a024-4fc4e5278803.usrfiles.com/ugd/9ba471_f81ef4e4b5f040038350270590eb2e42.pdf) terms if funded\n- [x] I agree to [Provide KYC information](https://9ba4718c-5c73-47c3-a024-4fc4e5278803.usrfiles.com/ugd/9ba471_7d9e73d16b584a61bae92282b208efc4.pdf) if funded above $50,000 USD\n- [x] I agree to disclose conflicts of interest\n- [x] I agree to adhere to the [Code of Conduct](https://forum.zcashcommunity.com/t/zcg-code-of-conduct/41787) and [Communication Guidelines](https://forum.zcashcommunity.com/t/zcg-communication-guidelines/44284)\n- [x] I understand all milestone deliverables will be validated and accepted by their intended users or their representatives, who will confirm that the deliverables meet the required quality, functionality, and usability for each user story.\n- [x] I agree that for any new open-source software, I will create a `CONTRIBUTING.md` file that reflects the high standards of Zcash development, using the [`librustzcash` style guides](https://github.com/zcash/librustzcash/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#styleguides) as a primary reference.\n- [x] I understand when contributing to existing Zcash code, I am required to adhere to the project specific contribution guidelines, paying close attention to any [merge](https://github.com/zcash/librustzcash/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#merge-workflow), [branch](https://github.com/zcash/librustzcash/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#branch-history), [pull request](https://github.com/zcash/librustzcash/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#pull-request-review), and [commit](https://github.com/zcash/librustzcash/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#commit-messages) guidelines as exemplified in the `librustzcash` repository.\n- [x] I agree to post request details on the [Community Forum](https://forum.zcashcommunity.com/c/grants/33)\n- [x] I understand it is my responsibility to post a link to this issue on the [Zcash Community Forums](https://forum.zcashcommunity.com/c/grants/33) after this application has been submitted so the community can give input. I understand this is required in order for ZCG to discuss and vote on this grant application.\n\n### Application Owners (@Octocat, @Octocat1)\n\nBatuhan\n\n### Organization Name\n\nZcash Turkiye\n\n### How did you learn about Zcash Community Grants\n\nActive participation in the Zcash ecosystem, serving as a member of the Zcash Türkiye team, and attending the Istanbul Blockchain event for two consecutive editions.\n\n### Requested Grant Amount (USD)\n\n6870\n\n### Category\n\nEvent Sponsorships\n\n### Project Lead\n\n```project-lead.yaml\nName:Batuhan\nRole: Team Leader\nBackground: More than 6 years of experience in the cryptocurrency sector; references in privacy-focused projects, and over a year of active work with the Zcash Türkiye team on privacy advocacy and project promotion.\nResponsibilities: Content , Social Media , Community\n```\n\n### Additional Team Members\n\n```team-members.yaml\n- Name:A.bulut7777\n   Role:CM / Social Media\n   Background: His main profession is Computer Programming but he has a high level of performance in the organization of many events that I have realized in Turkey in the last 2-3 years. Responsible, able to work actively in the field and has experience in creating content on social media & creating Youtube videos.\nHe has recently become a part of our strong team. In addition, we will be seeing him in front of the camera many times in our new initiative, Zbase.\n   Responsibilities:Social media content creation\nYoutube video Idea generator\nCommunity Support team\n\n- Name: Fatma \n   Role: Community Management, Women empowerment\n   Background: Fatma has actively worked behind the scenes at many crypto events. In the past, she has also taken part in various individual events. She was the unsung hero of the event where we distributed Ramadan food packages. Her ultimate goal is to eliminate the lack of knowledge among women regarding privacy and to introduce the opportunities offered by Zcash. During this period, she will organize at least one Privacy Women (Zcash) event every month.\n   Responsibilities: Content , Community , Social Media\n```\n\n### Project Summary\n\nThe Zcash team will participate in the **RLAY Hub** event, which will take place in Türkiye from **August 15–22, 2026**. During the first three days of the event, the team will actively engage with attendees by delivering a **presentation about Zcash**, hosting a **prize-based hackathon**, and organizing **community activities**.\n\n\n### Project Description\n\nRlay Blockchain Week 2026 is a blockchain education and developer event that brings together university students, software developers, entrepreneurs, and Web3 enthusiasts for an intensive week of technical learning and collaboration. As an Event Sponsor, Zcash will have the opportunity to introduce its privacy-focused technology directly to developers and new users who are shaping the future of the blockchain ecosystem. The sponsorship provides Zcash with strong brand visibility throughout the event and a dedicated day to organize its own activities.\n\nThe Zcash Türkiye team will actively participate during the first three days of the event. Our program will begin with a comprehensive technical presentation focused on Zcash. During the presentation, attendees will learn about the importance of financial privacy, Zcash's technology, and its real-world use cases. Our goal is not only to introduce Zcash but also to demonstrate, through technical explanations and practical examples, why privacy-preserving blockchain technology is essential.\n\nDuring the presentation, participants will be guided by our team through the installation of the ZODL Wallet and the creation of their first Zcash wallet. This hands-on onboarding process will ensure that attendees not only learn about Zcash but also become active participants in the ecosystem. Complimentary beverages will be served throughout the presentation, and Zcash-branded merchandise—including T-shirts, keychains, and other promotional items—will be distributed to create a memorable and engaging experience.\n\nFollowing the presentation, we will officially launch a 24-hour Zcash Hackathon for the developers attending the event. Participants will be invited to build applications, tools, or innovative use cases utilizing the Zcash ecosystem. Throughout the hackathon, our team will provide technical guidance and mentorship, while the most outstanding projects will receive prizes. This approach encourages developers not only to understand Zcash in theory but also to gain practical experience by building real projects.\n\nThis initiative is designed to be much more than a single presentation. Participants will first gain a technical understanding of Zcash, then immediately join the ecosystem by creating their own wallets, engage with the community throughout the event, and finally apply their knowledge during the hackathon. By combining education, hands-on onboarding, developer engagement, and community interaction, this project aims to increase Zcash's visibility in Türkiye, attract new users and developers to the ecosystem, and contribute to the long-term growth of a strong local Zcash community.\n\n### Proposed Problem\n\nAlthough Zcash holds a strong position among privacy-focused technologies, it is still not widely recognized by the broader public and is often only superficially understood, even in markets like Türkiye where cryptocurrency adoption is significant. The technology is mature and the necessary tools are readily available; however, there remains a lack of effective outreach and hands-on educational experiences, particularly for new users and local Web3 communities.\n\n\n### Proposed Solution\n\nThe Zcash Türkiye team will deliver a hands-on community activation at Rlay Blockchain Week 2026 that combines education, practical onboarding, and developer engagement.\n\nOur program will begin with a technical presentation introducing Zcash, the importance of financial privacy, and real-world applications of privacy-preserving technology. Rather than simply presenting the project, we will provide attendees with a practical understanding of how Zcash works and why it is relevant.\n\nDuring the session, participants will be guided through installing the ZODL Wallet and creating their first Zcash wallet. This hands-on onboarding experience will immediately connect attendees with the Zcash ecosystem while allowing our team to answer questions and provide technical assistance in person.\n\nTo encourage deeper engagement, complimentary refreshments and Zcash-branded merchandise will be distributed throughout the event, creating a welcoming environment and increasing participant interaction.\n\nFollowing the presentation, we will launch a 24-hour Zcash Hackathon for developers attending the event. Participants will be encouraged to build applications, tools, or integrations using the Zcash ecosystem, while our team provides mentorship and technical support throughout the competition. Prize incentives will reward the most innovative projects and motivate developers to continue exploring Zcash beyond the event.\n\nBy combining technical education, hands-on wallet onboarding, community engagement, and a developer-focused hackathon, this initiative transforms awareness into active participation. Rather than leaving attendees with only theoretical knowledge, the project creates meaningful first experiences with Zcash and establishes lasting connections between participants and the ecosystem.\n\n### Solution Format\n\nA dedicated Zcash event session featuring a technical presentation on financial privacy and the Zcash ecosystem.\nHands-on onboarding by assisting attendees with installing the ZODL Wallet and creating their first Zcash wallet, supported by Zcash-branded merchandise and refreshments.\nA time-limited, prize-based 24-hour Zcash Hackathon that encourages developers to build applications and explore the Zcash ecosystem.\nStrong on-site brand visibility through banners, roll-up displays, brochures, promotional materials, and a dedicated Zcash booth.\nSocial media coverage before, during, and after the event to amplify reach, showcase community engagement, and extend the impact beyond the attendees.\n\n### Dependencies\n\nApproval and confirmation of the Event Sponsorship package by the Rlay Blockchain Week organizers.\nAvailability of the Zcash Türkiye team to attend the event and execute the planned activities.\nTimely production and delivery of Zcash-branded promotional materials, including T-shirts, keychains, brochures, and roll-up banners.\nAvailability of the technical equipment and internet connectivity required for the presentation and wallet onboarding session.\nSufficient participation from developers and attendees in the hackathon and event activities.\n\n### Technical Approach\n\nA face-to-face engagement approach will be adopted throughout the project. The initiative will focus on three core components: a technical presentation, hands-on ZODL Wallet installation and onboarding, and a 24-hour hackathon for developers. Participants will have the opportunity to interact directly with the Zcash Türkiye team, gain technical knowledge, and become active members of the Zcash ecosystem through practical experience.\n\n### Upstream Merge Opportunities\n\nN/A\n\n### Hardware/Software Costs (USD)\n\n0\n\n### Hardware/Software Justification\n\n0\n\n### Service Costs (USD)\n\n5070\n\n### Service Costs Justification\n\nEvent Sponsorship – $1,800: Covers the official Event Sponsorship package, providing Zcash with a dedicated event session, on-site branding, and the opportunity to organize a technical presentation and community activities.\n\nHackathon Prize Pool – $500: Funds the prizes for the 24-hour Zcash Hackathon, encouraging developer participation and the creation of innovative projects using the Zcash ecosystem.\n\n\nCamera Equipment – $214: Covers the purchase of a camera to produce high-quality photos and videos for documentation, reporting, and promotional content.\n\nRefreshments – $267: Covers beverages for approximately 50 attendees during the Zcash presentation, creating a welcoming environment and encouraging participant engagement.\n\nPromotional Materials – $214: Covers the production of Zcash-branded T-shirts, keychains, brochures, and other promotional materials to increase brand visibility and provide attendees with lasting souvenirs.\n\nTransportation – $500: Covers round-trip travel expenses for the three-member Zcash Türkiye team, including fuel, toll roads, and transportation of promotional materials and technical equipment.\n\nAccommodation – $1,125: Covers three nights of accommodation for the three-member team, ensuring their presence throughout the event and hackathon.\n\nMeals – $450: Covers daily meal expenses for the three-member team during the event.\n\n### Compensation Costs (USD)\n\n1800\n\n### Compensation Costs Justification\n\n* **Team Compensation – $1,800:** Allocated for the work performed by the three-member Zcash Türkiye team throughout the event. The calculation is based on **3 team members × 3 days × 8 hours per day × $25 per hour = $1,800**. This budget covers event preparation, delivery of the technical presentation, hands-on ZODL Wallet onboarding, one-on-one participant engagement, hackathon organization and mentorship, and overall event coordination.\n\n\n### Total Budget (USD)\n\n6870\n\n### Previous Funding\n\nYes\n\n### Previous Funding Details\n\nhttps://github.com/ZcashCommunityGrants/zcashcommunitygrants/issues/163\nhttps://github.com/ZcashCommunityGrants/zcashcommunitygrants/issues/270\n\n### Other Funding Sources\n\nNo\n\n### Other Funding Sources Details\n\nN/A\n\n### Implementation Risks\n\nLow participant engagement risk\nIf attendee traffic at the event is lower than expected, it may negatively impact onboarding and engagement targets.\nMitigation: A proactive field team approach, continuous visitor outreach and guidance, and participation in side events and networking areas to increase overall reach.\n\nWeather, transportation, or logistical issues\nDelays may occur in team transportation to the event venue or in equipment delivery and setup.\nMitigation: Early departure planning, alternative transportation options, and ensuring all equipment is prepared and organized in advance to secure smooth logistics.\n\n### Potential Side Effects\n\nAfter booth visits and initial wallet setup, small amounts of ZEC rewards will be distributed to encourage users to continue using the platform. In addition, users will be encouraged to follow our social media channels and actively join the community.\n\nThese small ZEC rewards will help users explore the Zcash ecosystem more closely, conduct further research, and more easily access community support when performing any future transactions.\n\n### Success Metrics\n\n* New Zcash wallet installations and onboarded users.\n* Hackathon participants and projects developed during the competition.\n* Delivery of a technical presentation introducing Zcash and financial privacy.\n* New community connections, partnerships, and potential long-term collaborators.\n\n\n### Startup Funding (USD)\n\n6870\n\n### Startup Funding Justification\n\nEarly approval of the event sponsorship and signing the agreement are essential. This will allow us to secure accommodation in advance and ensure sufficient time to organize all event logistics and preparations effectively.\n\nMajor blockchain ecosystems such as **Avalanche** and **Stellar** are also participating as sponsors, and the number of sponsorship opportunities is limited. Reaching an agreement early will help secure Zcash's presence at the event while enabling our team to plan travel, logistics, promotional materials, and on-site activities well in advance, ensuring a high-quality execution.\n\n\n### Milestone Details\n\n```milestones.yaml\nNo milestones, only startup funding.\n```\n\n### Supporting Documents\n\n```files.yaml\n\n```","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ZcashCommunityGrants/zcashcommunitygrants/issues/346/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ZcashCommunityGrants/zcashcommunitygrants/issues/346/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/earnestmant2/mysql/issues/1","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/earnestmant2/mysql","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/earnestmant2/mysql/issues/1/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/earnestmant2/mysql/issues/1/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/earnestmant2/mysql/issues/1/events","html_url":"https://github.com/earnestmant2/mysql/issues/1","id":4804453116,"node_id":"I_kwDOTMtZR88AAAABHl4i_A","number":1,"title":"🎯 Fix: Prevent Session State Inconsistency on Connection Reset and driver.ErrBadConn Retry","user":{"login":"earnestmant2","id":299555191,"node_id":"U_kgDOEdrZdw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/299555191?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/earnestmant2","html_url":"https://github.com/earnestmant2","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/earnestmant2/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/earnestmant2/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/earnestmant2/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/earnestmant2/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/earnestmant2/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/earnestmant2/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/earnestmant2/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/earnestmant2/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/earnestmant2/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11409668767,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTMtZR88AAAACqBG6nw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/earnestmant2/mysql/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":11409668770,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTMtZR88AAAACqBG6og","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/earnestmant2/mysql/labels/opire","name":"opire","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":11409668771,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTMtZR88AAAACqBG6ow","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/earnestmant2/mysql/labels/$10","name":"$10","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":10,"created_at":"2026-07-03T14:58:37Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T15:14:21Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## 📝 Description\nWhen a MySQL connection is reset (e.g., due to a server-side timeout, TCP reset, or network disruption), the driver detects the failure and returns `driver.ErrBadConn`. The Go `database/sql` standard library automatically intercepts `driver.ErrBadConn` and retries the query on a new connection from the pool.\n\nHowever, if the connection reset occurs after session-specific states have been modified (such as DSN-configured system variables, session collations, or transaction states), the automatic retry on a new connection can lead to inconsistent states. Specifically:\n1. If the driver fails to fully re-initialize DSN-configured session variables (`system_vars`) on the new connection, queries will run with default server settings.\n2. If a connection reset occurs mid-transaction or after a write operation, returning `driver.ErrBadConn` might trigger an unsafe automatic retry of a non-idempotent query.\n3. Internal driver state (such as cached prepared statements or connection flags) may not be properly cleaned up when the connection is marked bad.\n\nWe need to ensure that connection resets are handled safely, session variables are consistently re-applied on retried connections, and `driver.ErrBadConn` is only returned when it is safe to retry the operation.\n\n## 🎯 Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] **Safe Retry Logic:** `driver.ErrBadConn` must only be returned if no data has been written to the connection for the current query, or if the connection was lost while idle in the pool. If a write has already occurred, the actual network error must be returned to prevent unsafe retries of non-idempotent operations.\n- [ ] **Session Variable Re-initialization:** Ensure that all DSN-configured session variables (e.g., `system_vars`, `sql_mode`, `time_zone`) are reliably executed and verified during the connection establishment phase of the new connection.\n- [ ] **State Cleanup:** When a connection is marked bad, all associated driver-side resources (e.g., cached prepared statements, transaction state flags) must be explicitly invalidated and cleared.\n- [ ] **Transaction Safety:** If a connection reset occurs during an active transaction, the driver must not return `driver.ErrBadConn` in a way that allows `database/sql` to silently retry the query on a new connection outside of the transaction context.\n\n## 🛠️ Technical Specifications & Context\n- **Relevant Files:**\n  - `connection.go`: Manages connection lifecycle, initialization, and state.\n  - `packets.go`: Handles reading/writing packets and error translation.\n  - `driver.go`: Implements the `driver.Driver` and `driver.Connector` interfaces.\n- **Key Functions to Modify/Inspect:**\n  - `mysqlConn.cleanup()`: Ensure it thoroughly invalidates prepared statements and resets internal state flags when a connection is closed or marked bad.\n  - `mysqlConn.handleError()`: Refine the logic that maps network errors (like `syscall.ECONNRESET`, `io.EOF`, or `write: connection reset by peer`) to `driver.ErrBadConn`.\n  - `connector.Connect()`: Verify that the initialization SQL queries (setting up `system_vars`, collation, etc.) are executed atomically before the connection is returned to the pool.\n- **Context:**\n  - Go's `database/sql` package relies on the driver returning `driver.ErrBadConn` to trigger its retry loop. If we return `driver.ErrBadConn` after a query has been partially sent, we risk duplicate execution. We must track whether a write operation has started on the wire for the current command.\n\n## 🧪 Verification & Testing\nHunter, please verify the fix using the following testing strategies:\n\n1. **Unit Test for Session Re-initialization:**\n   - Write a test in `connection_test.go` that establishes a connection with custom `system_vars` in the DSN (e.g., `system_vars=sql_mode='ANSI'`).\n   - Force a connection reset on the underlying net.Conn (e.g., by closing the raw TCP connection or using a mock net.Conn).\n   - Execute a subsequent query and assert that the new connection established by the pool successfully re-applies the `sql_mode='ANSI'` setting.\n\n2. **Integration Test for Unsafe Retries:**\n   - Simulate a connection reset mid-write.\n   - Verify that the driver returns the raw network error (or a wrapped error) instead of `driver.ErrBadConn`, preventing `database/sql` from retrying the query.\n\n3. **Mock Server Test:**\n   - Use a mock MySQL server to close the connection immediately after receiving a query header.\n   - Assert that the driver handles the `EOF` / `ECONNRESET` correctly based on whether the query was fully written.\n\n---\n\n[![Opire Bounty](https://img.shields.io/badge/bounty-Opire-emerald?style=for-the-badge)](https://github.com/earnestmant2/mysql)\n<br/>\n<hr/>\n\n<details><summary>This repo is using Opire - what does it mean? 👇</summary><br/>💵 Everyone can add rewards for this issue commenting <code>/reward 100</code> (replace <code>100</code> with the amount).<br/>🕵️‍♂️ If someone starts working on this issue to earn the rewards, they can comment <code>/try</code> to let everyone know!<br/>🙌 And when they open the PR, they can comment <code>/claim #1</code> either in the PR description or in a PR's comment.<br/><br/>🪙 Also, everyone can tip any user commenting <code>/tip 20 @earnestmant2</code> (replace <code>20</code> with the amount, and <code>@earnestmant2</code> with the user to tip).<br/><br/>📖 If you want to learn more, check out our <a href=\"https://docs.opire.dev\">documentation</a>.</details>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/earnestmant2/mysql/issues/1/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/earnestmant2/mysql/issues/1/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Markp1598M/Helm/issues/1","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Markp1598M/Helm","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Markp1598M/Helm/issues/1/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Markp1598M/Helm/issues/1/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Markp1598M/Helm/issues/1/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Markp1598M/Helm/issues/1","id":4796386631,"node_id":"I_kwDOTLv_088AAAABHeMNRw","number":1,"title":"🎯 Fix: --atomic rollback fails to trigger and leaves release in pending-upgrade state when post-upgrade hook times out","user":{"login":"Markp1598M","id":299205621,"node_id":"U_kgDOEdWD9Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/299205621?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Markp1598M","html_url":"https://github.com/Markp1598M","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Markp1598M/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Markp1598M/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Markp1598M/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Markp1598M/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Markp1598M/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Markp1598M/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Markp1598M/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Markp1598M/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Markp1598M/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11400365461,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTLv_088AAAACp4PFlQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Markp1598M/Helm/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":11400365466,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTLv_088AAAACp4PFmg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Markp1598M/Helm/labels/opire","name":"opire","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":11400365468,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTLv_088AAAACp4PFnA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Markp1598M/Helm/labels/$10","name":"$10","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":12,"created_at":"2026-07-02T16:34:26Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T15:14:20Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## 📝 Description\nWhen performing a Helm upgrade with the `--atomic` flag, the expected behavior is that any failure during the upgrade process—including hook failures or timeouts—will trigger an automatic rollback to the previous secure/successful release version. \n\nCurrently, if a `post-upgrade` hook times out during `helm upgrade --atomic`, the release is left abandoned in a `pending-upgrade` state. The atomic rollback mechanism is not triggered, requiring manual intervention (such as `helm rollback` or manually editing the release secret) to unblock subsequent deployments.\n\n## 🎯 Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] When `helm upgrade` is executed with the `--atomic` flag, any timeout or failure during the execution of `post-upgrade` hooks must trigger the automatic rollback process.\n- [ ] The release must not be left in a `pending-upgrade` state if the upgrade fails due to a hook timeout.\n- [ ] If the rollback succeeds, the release status must return to `deployed` at the previous revision.\n- [ ] If the rollback itself fails, the release status should be updated to `failed` (or the appropriate failure state), but must not remain in `pending-upgrade`.\n- [ ] If `--install` was used and there is no prior revision to roll back to, the release must be cleaned up/uninstalled as expected by the atomic install behavior.\n\n## 🛠️ Technical Specifications & Context\nIn the Helm codebase (specifically within the `Markp1598M/Helm` repository structure):\n- The upgrade logic is primarily driven by `pkg/action/upgrade.go`.\n- Inside `Upgrade.Run()`, the release is updated to `pending-upgrade` before hooks and resources are deployed.\n- The hook execution happens via the hook manager (e.g., `cfg.Releases.Update` and hook execution blocks).\n- If a hook fails or times out, an error is returned. The atomic rollback logic (which typically wraps the deployment and validation phases) must catch this hook execution error and invoke the rollback action (`cfg.Rollback`).\n- We need to ensure that the error returned by the `post-upgrade` hook execution path is not bypassed by the atomic error-handling block in `upgrade.go`.\n\nKey files to inspect:\n- `pkg/action/upgrade.go`: Look at the `Run` method, specifically where `post-upgrade` hooks are executed and how errors are handled when `cfg.Atomic` is true.\n- `pkg/action/rollback.go`: Ensure the rollback action can safely target a release that is currently marked as `pending-upgrade`.\n\n## 🧪 Verification & Testing\n\n### Manual Verification\n1. Create a test Helm chart with a `post-upgrade` hook job that sleeps indefinitely:\n   ```yaml\n   apiVersion: batch/v1\n   kind: Job\n   metadata:\n     name: timeout-hook\n     annotations:\n       \"helm.sh/hook\": post-upgrade\n   spec:\n     template:\n       spec:\n         containers:\n         - name: sleep\n           image: busybox\n           command: [\"sleep\", \"3600\"]\n         restartPolicy: Never\n   ```\n2. Deploy an initial successful version of the chart:\n   ```bash\n   helm install test-release ./test-chart\n   ```\n3. Perform an upgrade with a short timeout and the `--atomic` flag:\n   ```bash\n   helm upgrade test-release ./test-chart --atomic --timeout 20s\n   ```\n4. Verify that after 20 seconds, the upgrade times out, triggers a rollback, and `helm list` shows the release status as `deployed` at revision `1` (instead of `pending-upgrade` at revision `2`).\n\n### Automated Tests\n- Add a unit test in `pkg/action/upgrade_test.go` (e.g., `TestUpgradeAtomicPostUpgradeHookTimeout`) that mocks a failing/timing-out `post-upgrade` hook and asserts that the release history rolls back to the original revision.\n\n---\n\n[![Opire Bounty](https://img.shields.io/badge/bounty-Opire-emerald?style=for-the-badge)](https://github.com/Markp1598M/Helm)\n<br/>\n<hr/>\n\n<details><summary>This repo is using Opire - what does it mean? 👇</summary><br/>💵 Everyone can add rewards for this issue commenting <code>/reward 100</code> (replace <code>100</code> with the amount).<br/>🕵️‍♂️ If someone starts working on this issue to earn the rewards, they can comment <code>/try</code> to let everyone know!<br/>🙌 And when they open the PR, they can comment <code>/claim #1</code> either in the PR description or in a PR's comment.<br/><br/>🪙 Also, everyone can tip any user commenting <code>/tip 20 @Markp1598M</code> (replace <code>20</code> with the amount, and <code>@Markp1598M</code> with the user to tip).<br/><br/>📖 If you want to learn more, check out our <a href=\"https://docs.opire.dev\">documentation</a>.</details>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Markp1598M/Helm/issues/1/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Markp1598M/Helm/issues/1/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Markp1598M/cobra/issues/1","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Markp1598M/cobra","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Markp1598M/cobra/issues/1/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Markp1598M/cobra/issues/1/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Markp1598M/cobra/issues/1/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Markp1598M/cobra/issues/1","id":4799671634,"node_id":"I_kwDOTMIJhc8AAAABHhUtUg","number":1,"title":"🎯 Fix panic on duplicate shell completion registration for inherited persistent flags","user":{"login":"Markp1598M","id":299205621,"node_id":"U_kgDOEdWD9Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/299205621?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Markp1598M","html_url":"https://github.com/Markp1598M","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Markp1598M/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Markp1598M/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Markp1598M/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Markp1598M/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Markp1598M/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Markp1598M/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Markp1598M/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Markp1598M/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Markp1598M/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11404039988,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTMIJhc8AAAACp7vXNA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Markp1598M/cobra/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":11404039989,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTMIJhc8AAAACp7vXNQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Markp1598M/cobra/labels/opire","name":"opire","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":11404039990,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTMIJhc8AAAACp7vXNg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Markp1598M/cobra/labels/$10","name":"$10","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":13,"created_at":"2026-07-03T02:20:09Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T15:14:19Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## 📝 Description\nWhen using the Cobra library, registering a shell completion function for a persistent flag can cause a panic under certain conditions. Specifically, if a persistent flag is defined on a parent command and has a completion function registered, and a subcommand inherits this persistent flag, attempting to register a completion function for the same flag on the subcommand—or generating the shell completion scripts (Bash, Zsh, Fish, PowerShell) for the command tree—results in a runtime panic.\n\nThis panic typically occurs due to duplicate registration conflicts in the internal completion maps or nil pointer dereferences when traversing the command hierarchy to resolve flag completion functions.\n\n## 🎯 Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Registering a flag completion function via `RegisterFlagCompletionFunc` on a subcommand for an inherited persistent flag must not panic.\n- [ ] If a subcommand registers its own completion function for an inherited persistent flag, it should cleanly override the parent command's completion function for that subcommand and its children, without affecting the parent command's completion behavior.\n- [ ] Shell completion generation functions (e.g., `GenBashCompletionV2`, `GenZshCompletion`, `GenFishCompletion`, `GenPowerShellCompletion`) must execute successfully without panicking when the command tree contains inherited persistent flags with registered completion functions.\n- [ ] Comprehensive unit tests must be added to verify duplicate registration safety and correct resolution order (subcommand override vs. parent default).\n\n## 🛠️ Technical Specifications & Context\nIn `cobra`, flag completions are managed via the `Command` struct and its associated completion registration methods.\n\n### Key Files:\n- `command.go`: Contains `RegisterFlagCompletionFunc` and the command structure.\n- `shell_completions.go`: Contains the logic for resolving and executing completion functions during shell interaction.\n- `bash_v2.go`, `zsh.go`, `fish.go`, `powershell.go`: Script generation files that traverse the command tree and inspect flag completion functions.\n\n### Proposed Implementation Details:\n1. **Safe Registration in `command.go`**:\n   In `Command.RegisterFlagCompletionFunc(flagName string, f func(*Command, []string, string) ([]string, ShellCompDirective))`:\n   - Ensure the internal map `cmd.flagCompletionFuncs` is safely initialized.\n   - If the flag is an inherited persistent flag, allow the subcommand to register its own completion function in its local `flagCompletionFuncs` map. This should act as a local override.\n\n2. **Resolution Logic in `shell_completions.go`**:\n   When resolving a completion function for a flag:\n   - The resolution logic should traverse upwards from the target subcommand to the parent commands.\n   - It should return the first completion function found for the flag, starting from the subcommand where the execution was triggered. This ensures overrides are respected.\n   - Prevent duplicate registration panics in the shell script generators by ensuring they do not attempt to register the same flag completion key multiple times in global script scopes.\n\n## 🧪 Verification & Testing\n\n### Reproduction Test Case\nAdd a test case in `command_test.go` or `shell_completions_test.go` similar to the following:\n\n```go\nfunc TestSubcommandPersistentFlagCompletionNoPanic(t *testing.T) {\n    rootCmd := &Command{Use: \"root\"}\n    subCmd := &Command{Use: \"sub\"}\n    \n    rootCmd.PersistentFlags().String(\"config\", \"\", \"config file\")\n    rootCmd.AddCommand(subCmd)\n    \n    // Register on parent\n    err := rootCmd.RegisterFlagCompletionFunc(\"config\", func(cmd *Command, args []string, toComplete string) ([]string, ShellCompDirective) {\n        return []string{\"xml\", \"json\"}, ShellCompDirectiveDefault\n    })\n    if err != nil {\n        t.Fatalf(\"Failed to register completion on root: %v\", err)\n    }\n    \n    // Register override on subcommand (should not panic)\n    defer func() {\n        if r := recover(); r != nil {\n            t.Errorf(\"Registration on subcommand panicked: %v\", r)\n        }\n    }()\n    \n    err = subCmd.RegisterFlagCompletionFunc(\"config\", func(cmd *Command, args []string, toComplete string) ([]string, ShellCompDirective) {\n        return []string{\"yaml\", \"toml\"}, ShellCompDirectiveDefault\n    })\n    if err != nil {\n        t.Fatalf(\"Failed to register completion override on subcommand: %v\", err)\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Running Tests\nVerify the fix by running the package tests:\n```bash\ngo test -v ./...\n```\n\n---\n\n[![Opire Bounty](https://img.shields.io/badge/bounty-Opire-emerald?style=for-the-badge)](https://github.com/Markp1598M/cobra)\n<br/>\n<hr/>\n\n<details><summary>This repo is using Opire - what does it mean? 👇</summary><br/>💵 Everyone can add rewards for this issue commenting <code>/reward 100</code> (replace <code>100</code> with the amount).<br/>🕵️‍♂️ If someone starts working on this issue to earn the rewards, they can comment <code>/try</code> to let everyone know!<br/>🙌 And when they open the PR, they can comment <code>/claim #1</code> either in the PR description or in a PR's comment.<br/><br/>🪙 Also, everyone can tip any user commenting <code>/tip 20 @Markp1598M</code> (replace <code>20</code> with the amount, and <code>@Markp1598M</code> with the user to tip).<br/><br/>📖 If you want to learn more, check out our <a href=\"https://docs.opire.dev\">documentation</a>.</details>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Markp1598M/cobra/issues/1/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Markp1598M/cobra/issues/1/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MariauqmpsA333/go-redis/issues/1","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MariauqmpsA333/go-redis","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MariauqmpsA333/go-redis/issues/1/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MariauqmpsA333/go-redis/issues/1/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MariauqmpsA333/go-redis/issues/1/events","html_url":"https://github.com/MariauqmpsA333/go-redis/issues/1","id":4817005417,"node_id":"I_kwDOTO8UWs8AAAABHx2raQ","number":1,"title":"🎯 Fix Silent Message Delivery Failure on Pub/Sub Reconnection Resubscription Failure","user":{"login":"MariauqmpsA333","id":300345772,"node_id":"U_kgDOEebprA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/300345772?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MariauqmpsA333","html_url":"https://github.com/MariauqmpsA333","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MariauqmpsA333/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MariauqmpsA333/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MariauqmpsA333/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MariauqmpsA333/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MariauqmpsA333/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MariauqmpsA333/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MariauqmpsA333/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MariauqmpsA333/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MariauqmpsA333/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11431097886,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTO8UWs8AAAACqVi2Hg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MariauqmpsA333/go-redis/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":11431097889,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTO8UWs8AAAACqVi2IQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MariauqmpsA333/go-redis/labels/opire","name":"opire","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":11431097890,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTO8UWs8AAAACqVi2Ig","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MariauqmpsA333/go-redis/labels/$10","name":"$10","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":7,"created_at":"2026-07-06T07:39:22Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T15:14:18Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## 📝 Description\nWhen using the `go-redis` Pub/Sub client, the library automatically handles reconnection when the underlying Redis connection is lost. However, if the connection is successfully re-established but the subsequent automatic resubscription (`SUBSCRIBE` or `PSUBSCRIBE` commands) fails (e.g., due to a temporary Redis loading state, timeout, or authorization error during reconnection), the client silently stops delivering messages. \n\nCurrently, the internal loop continues to run, and the Go channel returned by `.Channel()` remains open, but it will never receive any new messages. The client's internal state becomes desynced from the actual Redis server subscription state, leading to silent data loss in production environments.\n\n## 🎯 Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] If a resubscription attempt fails during the automatic reconnection flow, the `PubSub` client must not fail silently.\n- [ ] Implement a configurable or robust retry mechanism with exponential backoff for failed resubscriptions.\n- [ ] If resubscription fails permanently (or exceeds a maximum retry threshold), the client must close the channel returned by `.Channel()` and surface the subscription error to the user (e.g., via a new error channel or by returning an error on `Receive()`).\n- [ ] Ensure that the internal state tracking subscribed channels/patterns (`channels` and `patterns` maps in the `PubSub` struct) remains consistent with the actual server-side subscription state.\n- [ ] Prevent goroutine leaks when reconnection/resubscription loops fail repeatedly.\n\n## 🛠️ Technical Specifications & Context\n- **Target File:** `/pubsub.go` (and associated test files like `/pubsub_test.go`).\n- **Key Structs & Methods:**\n  - `PubSub`: The main struct managing the Pub/Sub state.\n  - `PubSub.reconnect()`: Handles the reconnection logic.\n  - `PubSub.resubscribe()`: Iterates over existing subscriptions and sends the `SUBSCRIBE`/`PSUBSCRIBE` commands to the new connection.\n- **The Issue:** Currently, in `pubsub.go`, if `resubscribe()` returns an error during the `reconnect()` loop, the error may be logged or discarded, but the client does not tear down the channel or retry the subscription commands. The connection is marked as active, but the Redis server has no record of the subscriptions.\n- **Proposed Solution:**\n  - Modify `reconnect()` to check the result of `resubscribe()`.\n  - If `resubscribe()` fails, trigger a retry loop with backoff.\n  - If the retry limit is reached, close the message delivery channel and mark the `PubSub` client as closed/broken so the calling application can detect the failure and recreate the client.\n\n## 🧪 Verification & Testing\n- **Unit/Integration Tests:**\n  - Add a test case in `/pubsub_test.go` that simulates a connection drop.\n  - Mock the Redis server (or use a hook/interceptor) to fail the first few `SUBSCRIBE` commands after reconnection, then succeed. Verify that messages are eventually delivered once resubscription succeeds.\n  - Mock the Redis server to permanently fail the `SUBSCRIBE` command after reconnection. Verify that the channel returned by `pubsub.Channel()` is closed and an error is surfaced.\n- **Manual Verification:**\n  - Run a local Redis instance, subscribe to a channel, kill the connection, block the `SUBSCRIBE` command (e.g., using client ACLs or pausing the Redis instance), reconnect, and verify the client's behavior matches the acceptance criteria.\n\n---\n\n[![Opire Bounty](https://img.shields.io/badge/bounty-Opire-emerald?style=for-the-badge)](https://github.com/MariauqmpsA333/go-redis)\n<br/>\n<hr/>\n\n<details><summary>This repo is using Opire - what does it mean? 👇</summary><br/>💵 Everyone can add rewards for this issue commenting <code>/reward 100</code> (replace <code>100</code> with the amount).<br/>🕵️‍♂️ If someone starts working on this issue to earn the rewards, they can comment <code>/try</code> to let everyone know!<br/>🙌 And when they open the PR, they can comment <code>/claim #1</code> either in the PR description or in a PR's comment.<br/><br/>🪙 Also, everyone can tip any user commenting <code>/tip 20 @MariauqmpsA333</code> (replace <code>20</code> with the amount, and <code>@MariauqmpsA333</code> with the user to tip).<br/><br/>📖 If you want to learn more, check out our <a href=\"https://docs.opire.dev\">documentation</a>.</details>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MariauqmpsA333/go-redis/issues/1/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MariauqmpsA333/go-redis/issues/1/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xevrion-v2/agent-playground/issues/16","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xevrion-v2/agent-playground","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xevrion-v2/agent-playground/issues/16/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xevrion-v2/agent-playground/issues/16/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xevrion-v2/agent-playground/issues/16/events","html_url":"https://github.com/xevrion-v2/agent-playground/issues/16","id":4577274545,"node_id":"I_kwDOSvpFLM8AAAABENOqsQ","number":16,"title":"Agent Registry — Check in here before opening a PR","user":{"login":"xevrion-v2","id":254105479,"node_id":"U_kgDODyVXhw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254105479?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xevrion-v2","html_url":"https://github.com/xevrion-v2","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xevrion-v2/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xevrion-v2/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xevrion-v2/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xevrion-v2/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xevrion-v2/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xevrion-v2/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xevrion-v2/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xevrion-v2/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xevrion-v2/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":123,"created_at":"2026-06-03T05:51:43Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T14:59:14Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"👋 If you are an AI agent or automated system planning to open a PR,\nplease comment below before submitting.\n\nInclude:\n- Your model name / version\n- Which issue you are working on\n- Your approach\n\nThis helps us track contributions and award bounties correctly.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xevrion-v2/agent-playground/issues/16/reactions","total_count":203,"+1":200,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":2,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xevrion-v2/agent-playground/issues/16/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RevoraOrg/Revora-Contracts/issues/461","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RevoraOrg/Revora-Contracts","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RevoraOrg/Revora-Contracts/issues/461/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RevoraOrg/Revora-Contracts/issues/461/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RevoraOrg/Revora-Contracts/issues/461/events","html_url":"https://github.com/RevoraOrg/Revora-Contracts/issues/461","id":4725606178,"node_id":"I_kwDORSPDN88AAAABGasHIg","number":461,"title":"Add atomic close-of-period transaction sealing report, snapshot, and accrual in one entry","user":{"login":"thlpkee20-wq","id":258669950,"node_id":"U_kgDOD2r9fg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/258669950?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thlpkee20-wq","html_url":"https://github.com/thlpkee20-wq","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thlpkee20-wq/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thlpkee20-wq/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thlpkee20-wq/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thlpkee20-wq/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thlpkee20-wq/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thlpkee20-wq/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thlpkee20-wq/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thlpkee20-wq/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thlpkee20-wq/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10227524877,"node_id":"LA_kwDORSPDN88AAAACYZulDQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RevoraOrg/Revora-Contracts/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","color":"A2EEEF","default":true,"description":"New feature or request"},{"id":10243485984,"node_id":"LA_kwDORSPDN88AAAACYo8xIA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RevoraOrg/Revora-Contracts/labels/Stellar%20Wave","name":"Stellar Wave","color":"5555ff","default":false,"description":"Issues in the Stellar wave program"},{"id":10496458209,"node_id":"LA_kwDORSPDN88AAAACcaM94Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RevoraOrg/Revora-Contracts/labels/contracts","name":"contracts","color":"6F42C1","default":false,"description":""},{"id":10766266024,"node_id":"LA_kwDORSPDN88AAAACgbguqA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RevoraOrg/Revora-Contracts/labels/Soroban","name":"Soroban","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"morelucks","id":60940769,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwOTQwNzY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60940769?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks","html_url":"https://github.com/morelucks","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-06-23T12:01:36Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T14:40:03Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"morelucks","id":60940769,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwOTQwNzY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60940769?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks","html_url":"https://github.com/morelucks","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<!-- ghit#filepath: /Users/jagadeesh/adam/drips/revora/Revora-Contracts -->\n\n## Description\nSealing a period today requires several calls. Add `atomic_close_period(offering_id, period_id)` that finalizes the snapshot content_hash, accrual index, and report window in a single state-changing call so indexers see one boundary event rather than three.\n\n## Requirements and context\n- Must be secure, tested, and documented\n- Should be efficient and easy to review\n- Relevant code: `Revora-Contracts/src/lib.rs`, `Revora-Contracts/src/test_close_period.rs`\n- Must roll back atomically on any sub-step failure\n\n## Suggested execution\n- Fork the repo and create a branch\n- `git checkout -b feat/atomic-close-period`\n- Implement changes\n  - Combine snapshot finalize + accrual index commit + close_period guard\n  - Emit single `period_sealed` event with sub-hashes\n  - Document ordering invariants in CLOSE_PERIOD_FEATURE.md\n- Validate security and correctness assumptions\n\n## Test and commit\n- Run tests\n  - `cargo test --all`\n- Cover edge cases\n  - Failure in accrual commit must revert snapshot finalize and report seal\n- Include test output and security notes\n\n## Example commit message\n`feat: add atomic_close_period sealing snapshot, accrual, and report`\n\n## Guidelines\n- Minimum 95 percent test coverage\n- Clear documentation\n- **Timeframe:** 96 hours","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RevoraOrg/Revora-Contracts/issues/461/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RevoraOrg/Revora-Contracts/issues/461/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RevoraOrg/Revora-Contracts/issues/446","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RevoraOrg/Revora-Contracts","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RevoraOrg/Revora-Contracts/issues/446/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RevoraOrg/Revora-Contracts/issues/446/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RevoraOrg/Revora-Contracts/issues/446/events","html_url":"https://github.com/RevoraOrg/Revora-Contracts/issues/446","id":4725602873,"node_id":"I_kwDORSPDN88AAAABGar6OQ","number":446,"title":"Add multi-class share support (Class A/B) with per-class revenue-share BPS in register_offering","user":{"login":"thlpkee20-wq","id":258669950,"node_id":"U_kgDOD2r9fg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/258669950?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thlpkee20-wq","html_url":"https://github.com/thlpkee20-wq","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thlpkee20-wq/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thlpkee20-wq/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thlpkee20-wq/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thlpkee20-wq/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thlpkee20-wq/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thlpkee20-wq/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thlpkee20-wq/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thlpkee20-wq/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thlpkee20-wq/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10243485984,"node_id":"LA_kwDORSPDN88AAAACYo8xIA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RevoraOrg/Revora-Contracts/labels/Stellar%20Wave","name":"Stellar Wave","color":"5555ff","default":false,"description":"Issues in the Stellar wave program"},{"id":10496458209,"node_id":"LA_kwDORSPDN88AAAACcaM94Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RevoraOrg/Revora-Contracts/labels/contracts","name":"contracts","color":"6F42C1","default":false,"description":""},{"id":10766266024,"node_id":"LA_kwDORSPDN88AAAACgbguqA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RevoraOrg/Revora-Contracts/labels/Soroban","name":"Soroban","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":11049496314,"node_id":"LA_kwDORSPDN88AAAACkpnu-g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RevoraOrg/Revora-Contracts/labels/feature","name":"feature","color":"2DA44E","default":false,"description":""}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"morelucks","id":60940769,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwOTQwNzY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60940769?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks","html_url":"https://github.com/morelucks","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-06-23T12:01:10Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T13:50:42Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"morelucks","id":60940769,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwOTQwNzY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60940769?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks","html_url":"https://github.com/morelucks","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morelucks/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<!-- ghit#filepath: /Users/jagadeesh/adam/drips/revora/Revora-Contracts -->\n\n## Description\nThe current offering model assumes a single uniform share class for all holders. Many real-world revenue-share offerings issue Class A/B shares with distinct economic and voting profiles. Add a `ShareClass` enum and per-class BPS allocations so distributions split correctly without bolting a parallel offering registration on top.\n\n## Requirements and context\n- Must be secure, tested, and documented\n- Should be efficient and easy to review\n- Relevant code: `Revora-Contracts/src/lib.rs`\n- Wire per-class BPS into `compute_share` and `report_revenue` while keeping single-class offerings backward compatible\n\n## Suggested execution\n- Fork the repo and create a branch\n- `git checkout -b feat/multi-class-shares`\n- Implement changes\n  - Add `ShareClass { A, B, Custom(Symbol) }` and `ClassConfig { bps: u32, voting: bool }`\n  - Extend `register_offering` to accept `Option<Vec<ClassConfig>>` summing to 10_000 bps\n  - Update `compute_share` to dispatch on holder class and aggregate per-class subtotals\n- Validate security and correctness assumptions\n\n## Test and commit\n- Run tests\n  - `cargo test --all`\n- Cover edge cases\n  - Class BPS sum != 10_000 must fail with a typed error and emit no events\n- Include test output and security notes\n\n## Example commit message\n`feat: add multi-class share support with per-class BPS distribution`\n\n## Guidelines\n- Minimum 95 percent test coverage\n- Clear documentation\n- **Timeframe:** 96 hours","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RevoraOrg/Revora-Contracts/issues/446/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RevoraOrg/Revora-Contracts/issues/446/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chatmcp/mcpso/issues/1","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chatmcp/mcpso","labels_url":"https://